#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cc-docs — the document register: numbers, stamps and files every PDF the box finishes for its owner.

A number is PPP-NNNN-R. PPP is the project, given the next free number in its range the first time a document is
filed under it (work 001-099, course 101-199, member 901-999), so a document's category is in its number; NNNN, four digits, is the document within the project, in filing
order; R is the revision, A for the first finished version and the next letter for each finished version whose
content differs from the last (I and O are skipped, and after Z comes AA). A filed copy is named
`PPP-NNNN-R_<slug>.pdf`, is written once, read-only, and never rewritten.

    cc-docs file <pdf> --project <name|PPP> --title <t> [--source <path>] [--latex <main.tex>] [--no-stamp]
                 [--kind work|course|member] [--member <handle>] [--date YYYY-MM-DD]
                 [--describes PCB-NNNN-R] [--note <text>] [--cost <step>=<usd>]… [--attach <file>]…
        Called by a maker at the end of a finished build. The same source path, or else the same title in the same
        project, is the same document. Content unchanged since the current revision files nothing and prints that
        revision; otherwise the next letter is filed. A PDF whose text carries no number gets a small grey stamp
        `PPP-NNNN-R · 24 Sep 2026` bottom-left on every page, appended to the PDF rather than re-rendering it, so its
        links, outline and metadata survive (a PDF the appender cannot read is re-rendered and loses them, with a
        warning); one that already carries its own number (a LaTeX build that took it from `number`) is filed as it
        is; one carrying a different number is refused. --no-stamp is for
        a document that must not show a number (a resume, anything going outside): it is kept on the document, so its
        later revisions are not stamped either. A new project needs --kind, --member (a member project, visible to
        that member's workspace and the owner) or a project created first with `project`. Prints `<number>\t<path>` and whether
        it filed or found the content unchanged. The rest is recorded on the revision it files, and nothing is recorded
        when nothing is filed: --describes the board revision a document is about (a board's part number, PCB-0001-B),
        which the stamp then carries too, as `002-0012-A · PCB-0001-B · 24 Sep 2026`; --note what changed, in the
        filer's own words (the message it would post about this revision; the library shows it to the owner once, in a
        pop-up, when they next open the document); --cost, once per step, what the maker spent generating it in US dollars (`--cost draft=0.80 --cost review=0.43`).
        A filed revision also keeps its SOURCE, as sources/PPP/PPP-NNNN-R.tar.gz beside files/: for a LaTeX build (the
        --latex file, else a --source ending .tex, else a .tex of the PDF's own name beside it) the .tex and every
        local file it pulls in (\\input, \\include, figures, .bib, .bst and a .sty/.cls beside it, a file outside
        its directory under _ext/), else the --source file alone; at most 48 MiB, the rest listed on stderr. A figure
        named through a macro (`\\sysfig{…}{00-overview}`) is any braced argument that is a picture beside the .tex, in
        its \\graphicspath or in a folder beside it. A file \\input or included that is not beside the .tex but is
        under a directory above it (a build run from there: `reports/schematic.pdf` in reports/design_doc/x.tex) is
        packed as _cwd/<its name as written>, and _cwd named in texinputs. A .tex that reaches up
        (`\\input{../Inc/head.tex}`) is kept rooted at the nearest folder under ~ holding it and all it reaches, the
        main in its own folder there (`asic/cv.tex`); the editor compiles it from that folder. A fontspec Path=
        folder is packed with every .otf/.ttf in it. A package,
        class or \\input not beside the .tex is looked for next in the DOCS_TEX_TREES style trees (packed under
        _style/<its path under ROOT>, with every .otf/.ttf under that ROOT, and _style/SUB named in texinputs), then
        through kpsewhich, whose find under ~ is packed at the tarball's root by its name, where TeX finds it. Neither
        is asked for a member's filing. A LaTeX source carries .source.json at its root: {"main": its .tex, "engine":
        pdflatex|lualatex|xelatex, "texinputs": [...] when there are any}. The engine is the one a `% !TEX program =`
        line in the main's first 20 lines names, else lualatex when a kept .tex/.sty/.cls loads fontspec or
        unicode-math, else pdflatex. It is kept only once it COMPILES: the tarball is packed aside and DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK
        run on it; when that fails and no line pinned the engine, it is packed and checked once more with the other
        of pdflatex and lualatex. What passes is moved into place and the revision records source_main, source_engine
        and source_checked (UTC); what fails keeps nothing and says `cc-docs: <number>: source not kept, it does not
        compile: <path>:<line>: <first error>` on stderr, and the PDF is filed all the same. A source with no .tex (a
        lone --source), or any source while DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK is unset, is kept unchecked. With DOCS_CHECK_CHANNEL
        set, a filing that files a revision starts `cc-docs check --post` detached. It records WHO FILED it
        (filer: repo, session, cc-slack target, Slack channel and thread) from the track worktree, orch alias or
        ~/dev/<repo> the filing ran under. --attach, once per file, adds SUPPORTING FILES (below) to the revision
        it files, or to the current one when the content is unchanged; one that `attach` would refuse refuses the
        whole call before anything is filed. A new revision marks its document's open feedback (feedback.json, written
        by the box's library poller) done, "answered by rev X", for the poller to tell the site.
    cc-docs attach <PPP-NNNN | PPP-NNNN-R> [<file>…] [--replace] [--remove <name>]…
        SUPPORTING FILES: files kept beside a revision's PDF (a board's Gerbers, drill files, BOM, a zip), shown on
        its document page to whoever can open that revision, each downloadable and all of them as one zip. Each is
        kept once by content as attachments/<sha256[:2]>/<sha256>, read-only, and listed on the revision (PPP-NNNN
        names the current one) as {name, blob, bytes, sha256, crc32, added}; the name is the file's own (letters,
        digits, space, ._+()-). A name already there with the same bytes is left as it is, and with other bytes it
        is refused unless --replace; --remove takes a name off the revision. Refused, saying which cap and with
        nothing attached: a directory (name its files), a file over 25 MiB (what Cloudflare Pages serves), over 100
        on one revision, or every supporting file in the register, counted once each, past 1 GiB (the mirror's GitHub
        repo). A NEW REVISION CARRIES the one before's files (each marked carried_from), except a name its own
        --attach gives, and carries none when it --describes a different board revision than the one before did;
        stderr says which it carried or left. Prints `<number>\t<name>\tattached|unchanged|replaced|removed`.
        For each document's current revision that keeps no source, or keeps a LaTeX one with no .source.json, or one
        that fails DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK (a pass cached in checks.json is not compiled again), keeps what its recorded
        --source finds now, by the same rules and the same check as `file`; an existing tarball that fails again is
        left as it is, and so is one holding a file whose bytes the re-found source no longer has (`not kept\tsource
        changed since filing: <files>`): a re-keep adds to the source kept at filing, never replaces it. --from names the .tex of documents, one `PPP-NNNN<TAB>/abs/path.tex[<TAB>nearest]` a line ('#'
        comments and a path of `none` skipped), and becomes a document's --source when its own is unrecorded or gone;
        `nearest` records source_nearest on the revision it keeps: the nearest source found, not an exact match. Prints
        `<number>\tkept|not kept|no source\t<detail>` per document it tried.
    cc-docs check [--post]
        Compiles every document's kept source (current revision) with DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK, which must be set, and lists
        each problem as `<number>\t<kind>\t<detail>`: `no source`, `no .tex` (kept, but nothing to compile), `fails`
        (its first error) or `cannot check` (the check did not run); then `missing TeX packages: …` from the
        failures, and `N of M kept sources compile` over those with a .tex. Exit 1 when there is any problem. A pass
        is cached by the tarball's sha256 in checks.json beside the register, and a failure is compiled again each
        time. Two checks never run together: the second says so and exits 0. --post sends a summary under 800
        characters (counts, the failing numbers, the missing packages) with `cc-slack post -c <DOCS_CHECK_CHANNEL>
        --id docs-check-<digest>-<minute> --major` (CC_SLACK_BIN names another binary) when there are problems and
        they differ from the last post's or that post is over 20 hours old, and records it in checks.json; with
        DOCS_CHECK_CHANNEL unset nothing is posted.
    cc-docs number --project <name|PPP> --title <t> [--source <path>] [--describes PCB-NNNN-R] [--tex]
        The number `file` would give a changed build of this document now, for a build that prints its own footer:
        plain, or with --tex as `\\def\\docnumber{…}\\def\\docstamp{… · 24 Sep 2026}` to \\input before compiling.
        It reserves nothing, and a build whose content turns out unchanged is not filed.
    cc-docs project <name> [--number PPP] [--kind work|course|member] [--member <handle>]
        Create a project (at PPP, or the next free number in its kind's range), or print an existing one. A name
        Group/Name (`Career/Cover letter`) is a project under a parent group: a group is a name, not a number, and
        each of its projects has a PPP of its own, of the kind the group's other projects share when --kind is left
        out. Anywhere a project is named, Group/Name finds it, and so does its bare name when no other group has one.
        A group's own name is not a project, so `file --project <group>` is refused and names its projects, and a
        Group/Name is refused while a project outside any group has the group's name (rename that one into it
        first). Given a group's name, `project` lists its projects.
    cc-docs project <name|PPP> --rename <Group/Name | name>
        Rename a project or put it in a group (`project 006 --rename Career/Resume`). Its number, documents and
        files stay as they are.
    cc-docs pdf <PPP-NNNN-R> <pdf>
        A TEXT REVISION'S PDF: gives a revision filed without a PDF (a Markdown one, whose PDF a renderer makes after
        it is filed) that PDF, stamped and kept as `file` keeps one, and records its print, pages and bytes on that
        revision. A revision that has its PDF is refused. A host command, never a workspace's.
    cc-docs find <PPP-NNNN | PPP-NNNN-R | words…>
        The file of a document's current revision (or of the exact revision named), found by number, title or
        words in the title, project name or source path. Several equally good matches are listed to stderr, exit 3;
        none, exit 1.
    cc-docs list [--project <name|PPP|group>]
        One line per document: number of the current revision, date, visibility, title. A group lists every
        document under its projects.
    cc-docs star <PPP-NNNN> on|off [--viewer owner|<workspace id>]
        Star or unstar a document for one viewer (the owner by default). Stars are per viewer, and a viewer can
        star only a document visible to it.
    cc-docs public <PPP-NNNN-R> on|off
        On gives that one revision a public link: an unguessable token, printed, kept while it stays public (on
        again prints the same one). Off deletes the token for good, so the old link never works again and on
        afterwards mints a different one. The register's owner runs this; nobody else may. With DOCS_PUBLIC_HOOK
        set, on also hands the token to it and prints the address it answers on a second line (exit 1, token
        kept, when it fails: on again retries), and off stops the served link first and refuses, changing
        nothing, when it can't.
    cc-docs token <token> <PPP-NNNN-R>
        The filed copy a public link serves: printed only when the token is that revision's, exit 1 otherwise.
    cc-docs library --viewer owner|<workspace id>
        Everything that viewer may see, as JSON: projects (and the group of each that has one), documents,
        per-viewer star, and per revision its date, note, file, pages, bytes, board revision and cost. The owner
        sees the whole register, each public revision's token and, on a revision a workspace filed, filed_by (its
        handle); a member sees only documents visible to its workspace, its own stars, and no tokens. A workspace's
        note is at most 2000 characters.
        Any other viewer is refused.
    cc-docs member <handle> [--files <dir>]
        The host's half of filing from inside a member workspace, run by the Slack daemon for its member verb `docs`
        (below): one ask as JSON on stdin, {"ok", "text"|"error"} on stdout. Nobody else calls it.
    cc-docs fold <keep PPP-NNNN> <other PPP-NNNN>…
        Makes the other documents revisions of <keep>, for old versions filed as documents of their own. Every revision
        of them all is ordered oldest first by date (ties by the order given) with <keep>'s current revision last, so
        the next build of its source still matches it, and relettered A, B, C…; refused when another revision is dated
        after it. <keep> keeps its title, source, visibility and stars. The filed copies are renamed to match (their
        bytes, and any stamp printed in them, are not rewritten), a revision whose number changed loses its public
        link, and the other numbers are retired. All must be in one project, none with a retired revision. Prints
        `<old number>\t<new number>\t<path>` per revision.
    cc-docs retire <PPP-NNNN | PPP-NNNN-R>
        Takes a document (or one revision; its last revision retires the document) out of the register, its member
        views and its public link, for a document filed by mistake. Its filed copies move under retired/files/.
    cc-docs move <PPP-NNNN> <project> [--kind work|course|member]
        Renumbers a document into another project, made the way `file --project` makes one when it does not exist:
        it takes that project's next number, keeps its letters, title, source, stars and history, and records the
        old number in its moved_from. Its filed copies and kept sources are renamed to match (their bytes, and any
        stamp printed in them, are not rewritten), feedback left on the old number is answered by its next revision
        under the new one, each public link stops working, and the old number is retired. A move that would
        change who can see the document (to or from a member's project) is refused. Prints
        `<old number>\t<new number>\t<path>` per revision.
    cc-docs selfcheck

INSIDE A MEMBER WORKSPACE (CC_MEMBER_SANDBOX=1) the register is that member's read-only view, so `file` and `number`
cross the workspace's own socket (~/.cc/slack/sock inside) as the daemon's member verb `docs`, the way `cc-mail send`
does, and print the host's line. --project may be left out there. The host files under the workspace's own member
project: the one the ask names when it is that member's, else that member's first, else a new one named after the
handle. It takes the handle from the socket and never from the ask; refuses another member's project or --member,
a PDF or --source outside the workspace's own trees (~/dev/<h>, its track worktrees, its Slack files), a file that
is not a PDF, and one over 64 MiB; reads the PDF from one fd so it cannot be swapped between the check and the
read; and ignores --kind. A project an owner's maker names that is not the member's files under the member's own
instead, so a build that sets DOC_PROJECT still files. `project`, `star`, `public`, `token`, `fold`, `retire`,
`move`, `attach`, `backfill-sources` and `check` are refused inside, and so is `file --attach`.

THE REGISTER is one JSON file, $CC_DOCS_ROOT/register.json (default ~/.cc/documents), with the filed copies under
files/PPP/ beside it: private state, in no repo, and outside cc-lib's own tree (cc-lib indexes the register). Per
project it holds the name, the parent group (`group`, null for none: the site groups projects by it), kind, member
and workspace. Per document it holds number, title, project, source, visibility (the owner, or the owner and one member), who starred
it (starred_by, viewer ids), and per revision the letter, file, date, the PDF it was filed from, a content
fingerprint, and when given the note, board revision, cost, public token, filer, supporting files (attachments) and its kept source (sources/,
source_files, and for LaTeX source_main, source_engine and, once checked, source_checked). A member view carries neither the token nor the filer. The
fingerprint hashes the PDF's text with any document stamp taken out together with every page rendered small and grey
with its bottom strip (stamp, footer) cut off, so a rebuild that changes only a figure is a new revision and one that
differs only in its stamp, footer or bytes is unchanged; a PDF neither can read falls back to its bytes. A revision
filed with the older text-only print still matches an unchanged rebuild. Writes hold a lock and replace the file whole.

VISIBILITY is keyed by workspace id, the one cc-lib keys its indexes by (~/.cc/members/<handle>/workspace-id, minted
by cc-sandbox or cc-lib, never here): a member project records its member's id, and each of its documents is visible
to ["owner", <id>]. The owner sees the whole register. A member workspace gets a VIEW, ws/<id>/ under the root, and
never the register itself: a register of the same shape holding only the documents that name its id, with their
filed copies and supporting files hard-linked beside it (a supporting file it no longer names is unlinked), so `CC_DOCS_ROOT=<the view> cc-docs find …` works inside it unchanged. `file`
rewrites the views its document reaches after every filing, in place (a bind mount of the directory keeps seeing
them), so the directory can be mounted read-only into that member's sandbox the way cc-lib mounts ws/<id>/. A
star or a public switch rewrites them too. A view never carries a public token.

CONFIG (cc-config keys, read through this repo's own cc-config, else the one on PATH; the environment wins):
DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK, the compile check, a command split like a shell line and run as `<cmd> [--engine E] <tarball>`:
it prints one JSON {ok, engine, main, errors: [{path, line, message}], missing: [...], log_tail} and exits 0 when it
compiled, 1 when it did not, anything else when it could not run; it has 120 s. Unset, a source is kept unchecked
and `check` refuses. DOCS_TEX_TREES, the house styles, space-separated ROOT:SUB entries (a maker puts ROOT/SUB on
TEXINPUTS recursively). DOCS_CHECK_CHANNEL, where `check --post` posts; unset, it posts nothing and a filing starts
no check. DOCS_PUBLIC_HOOK, where public links are served, a command split like a shell line and run as
`<cmd> on|off <token> <PPP-NNNN-R>` with 30 s: `public` calls it both ways; `fold` calls it off for each token it drops
and refuses, folding nothing, when that fails (a letter it frees goes to another revision); `move` and `retire` call it
off after and say on stderr how to finish by hand when it fails. Unset, a token is only the register's.

RETIRED numbers (`fold`, `retire`, `move`) are kept in the register's `retired`, and a retired revision's letter in its
document's `retired_revs`, so neither is handed out again. What either verb takes out of the register is kept as
retired/<number>.json beside it, and nothing is deleted.
"""
import datetime
import fcntl
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import secrets
import shlex
import shutil
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time
import zlib

ROOT = os.environ.get("CC_DOCS_ROOT") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".cc", "documents")
MEMBERS = os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".cc", "members")
RANGES = {"work": (1, 99), "course": (101, 199), "member": (901, 999)}
LETTERS = "ABCDEFGHJKLMNPQRSTUVWXYZ"   # I and O are skipped: they read like 1 and 0
NUM = re.compile(r"^(\d{3})-(\d{4})(?:-([A-HJ-NP-Z]{1,3}))?$")
BOARD = re.compile(r"^PCB-\d{4}-[A-HJ-NP-Z]{1,3}$")   # a board's part number and hardware revision
STAMP = re.compile(r"\b\d{3}-\d{4}-[A-HJ-NP-Z]{1,3}\b(?:\s*·\s*PCB-\d{4}-[A-HJ-NP-Z]{1,3}\b)?"
                   r"(?:\s*·\s*\d{1,2} [A-Z][a-z]{2} \d{4})?")
STEP = re.compile(r"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,39}$")
WID = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{16}$")
STOP = set("a an the of for and or to in on my me get find doc document pdf".split())


class Refused(Exception):
    pass


def letter(i):
    """0 -> A, 23 -> Z, 24 -> AA: bijective base 24 over LETTERS."""
    s = ""
    i += 1
    while i:
        i, r = divmod(i - 1, len(LETTERS))
        s = LETTERS[r] + s
    return s


def slugify(t):
    return re.sub(r"[^a-z0-9]+", "-", t.lower()).strip("-")[:60].strip("-") or "document"


def stampdate(d):
    return f"{d.day} {d.strftime('%b %Y')}"


# ── the register ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def regpath():
    return os.path.join(ROOT, "register.json")


def load():
    try:
        with open(regpath()) as f:
            return json.load(f)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return {"version": 1, "projects": {}, "documents": {}}


def save(reg):
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=ROOT, prefix=".register.")
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
        json.dump(reg, f, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
        f.write("\n")
    os.replace(tmp, regpath())


class Lock:
    def __enter__(self):
        os.makedirs(ROOT, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
        self.f = open(os.path.join(ROOT, ".lock"), "w")
        fcntl.flock(self.f, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        return self

    def __exit__(self, *a):
        self.f.close()


def split_name(name):
    """'Career/Cover letter' -> ('Career', 'Cover letter'); a name with no group -> (None, name)."""
    g, s, n = (name or "").partition("/")
    return (g.strip(), n.strip()) if s else (None, (name or "").strip())


def full_name(pd):
    return f"{pd['group']}/{pd['name']}" if pd.get("group") else pd["name"]


def group_projects(reg, group):
    """-> [PPP] of the projects under a group, by number; [] when no project names it."""
    return sorted(p for p, d in reg["projects"].items() if (d.get("group") or "").lower() == (group or "").lower())


def find_project(reg, name):
    """A project by PPP, by Group/Name, or by its bare name when only one project has it."""
    if re.fullmatch(r"\d{3}", name or ""):
        return name if name in reg["projects"] else None
    g, n = split_name(name)
    hits = sorted(p for p, d in reg["projects"].items() if d["name"].lower() == n.lower()
                  and (g is None or (d.get("group") or "").lower() == g.lower()))
    if len(hits) > 1:
        raise Refused(f"{name!r} is " + " and ".join(full_name(reg["projects"][p]) for p in hits) + ": name its group")
    return hits[0] if hits else None


def make_project(reg, name, number=None, kind=None, member=None):
    """-> PPP, existing or new. A new one takes --number, or the next free number in its kind's range. A name
    Group/Name makes it a project of that group, of the kind its group's projects share when none is given."""
    p = find_project(reg, number or name)
    if p:
        if number and full_name(reg["projects"][p]).lower() != name.lower():
            raise Refused(f"project {p} is already {full_name(reg['projects'][p])!r}")
        return p
    if find_project(reg, name):
        raise Refused(f"project {name!r} already has number {find_project(reg, name)}")
    group, sub = split_name(name)
    if not sub or group == "":
        raise Refused(f"project name {name!r} needs a name on each side of the /")
    if group is None and group_projects(reg, sub):
        raise Refused(f"{sub!r} is a group: file under {sub}/<project> ("
                      + ", ".join(reg["projects"][p]["name"] for p in group_projects(reg, sub)) + ")")
    if group is not None:
        flat = find_project(reg, group)
        if flat and not reg["projects"][flat].get("group"):
            raise Refused(f"project {flat} is named {group!r}: put it in the group first, "
                          f"`cc-docs project {flat} --rename '{group}/<its name>'`")
        kinds = {reg["projects"][q]["kind"] for q in group_projects(reg, group)}
        kind = kind or (kinds.pop() if len(kinds) == 1 else None)
    if member:
        kind = kind or "member"
    if number:
        n = int(number)
        kind = kind or next((k for k, (a, b) in RANGES.items() if a <= n <= b), None)
        if kind not in RANGES or not RANGES[kind][0] <= n <= RANGES[kind][1]:
            raise Refused(f"project number {number} is outside the {kind or 'known'} ranges")
    elif kind in RANGES:
        a, b = RANGES[kind]
        n = next((i for i in range(a, b + 1) if f"{i:03d}" not in reg["projects"]), None)
        if n is None:
            raise Refused(f"the {kind} range is full")
    else:
        raise Refused(f"no project {name!r}: give --kind work|course|member, --member or --number to create it")
    if kind == "member" and not member:
        raise Refused("a member project needs --member <handle>: it is visible to that member and the owner")
    p = f"{n:03d}"
    reg["projects"][p] = {"name": sub, "group": group, "kind": kind, "member": member if kind == "member" else None,
                          "workspace": workspace_id(member) if kind == "member" else None,
                          "created": datetime.date.today().isoformat()}
    return p


def workspace_id(handle):
    """A member's workspace id, as cc-lib reads it: 16 hex in a regular file. None of it is minted here."""
    f = os.path.join(MEMBERS, handle, "workspace-id")
    try:
        wid = "" if os.path.islink(f) else open(f).read().strip()
    except OSError:
        wid = ""
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{16}", wid):
        raise Refused(f"member {handle!r} has no workspace id at {f}; its workspace must exist before its documents")
    return wid


def write_views(reg, ids):
    """Each workspace id in ids gets ws/<id>/: a register of the documents visible to it, and their files linked in."""
    for wid in sorted(ids):
        v = os.path.join(ROOT, "ws", wid)
        os.makedirs(v, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
        # a view never carries a public token: only the owner can see or kill a public link
        # nor who filed it: the owner's own sessions and channels are no workspace's business
        docs = {n: dict(d, revisions=[{k: v for k, v in r.items() if k not in ("public_token", "filer")}
                                      for r in d["revisions"]])
                for n, d in reg["documents"].items() if wid in d.get("visibility", ())}
        blobs = set()
        for d in docs.values():
            for r in d["revisions"]:
                blobs.update(x["blob"] for x in r.get("attachments") or ())
                # a text revision filed before its PDF (`pdf`, below) has no file yet
                for rel in ([r["file"]] if r.get("file") else []) + sorted(x["blob"] for x in r.get("attachments") or ()):
                    dst = os.path.join(v, rel)
                    if not os.path.exists(dst):
                        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
                        os.link(os.path.join(ROOT, rel), dst)
        # a supporting file no document in the view names any more (removed, retired, moved away) leaves it
        for top, _, names in os.walk(os.path.join(v, "attachments")):
            for fn in names:
                if os.path.relpath(os.path.join(top, fn), v) not in blobs:
                    os.unlink(os.path.join(top, fn))
        view = {"version": reg["version"], "documents": docs,
                "projects": {p: reg["projects"][p] for p in sorted({d["project"] for d in docs.values()})}}
        fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=v, prefix=".register.")
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
            json.dump(view, f, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
            f.write("\n")
        os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(v, "register.json"))


def match_doc(reg, proj, title, source):
    """The same source path, else the same title in the same project, is the same document.
    Brief: "same source path or title = same document"."""
    if source:
        for num, d in reg["documents"].items():
            if d.get("source") == source:
                if proj and d["project"] != proj:
                    raise Refused(f"{source} is already {num}, under project {d['project']}, not {proj}")
                return num
    for num, d in reg["documents"].items():
        if d["project"] == proj and d["title"].lower() == title.lower():
            return num
    return None


def next_doc(reg, proj):
    used = [int(n.split("-")[1]) for n, d in reg["documents"].items() if d["project"] == proj]
    used += [int(n.split("-")[1]) for n in reg.get("retired", {}) if n.startswith(proj + "-")]   # never handed out again
    return f"{proj}-{max(used, default=0) + 1:04d}"


def current(d):
    return d["revisions"][-1] if d["revisions"] else None


# ── the PDF ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def pdftext(path):
    r = subprocess.run(["pdftotext", "-q", path, "-"], capture_output=True, text=True)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        raise Refused(f"{path}: pdftotext could not read it ({r.stderr.strip()[:200]})")
    return r.stdout


def textprint(text):
    """The text-only fingerprint the first register was filed with, or None for a PDF with no text."""
    body = " ".join(STAMP.sub(" ", text).split())
    return "text:" + hashlib.sha256(body.encode()).hexdigest() if body else None


def pageprint(path):
    """A hash of every page rendered small and grey with its bottom strip cut off, where a stamp or a footer sits,
    so a changed figure changes it and a changed stamp does not. None when the pages cannot be rendered."""
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="cc-docs-fp-") as t:
        r = subprocess.run(["pdftoppm", "-r", "36", "-gray", path, os.path.join(t, "p")], capture_output=True)
        names = sorted(os.listdir(t), key=lambda x: int(re.sub(r"\D", "", x) or 0))
        if r.returncode != 0 or not names:
            return None
        h = hashlib.sha256()
        for name in names:
            with open(os.path.join(t, name), "rb") as f:
                m = re.match(rb"P5\s+(\d+)\s+(\d+)\s+\d+\s", f.read(64))
                if not m:
                    return None
                f.seek(m.end())
                w, rows = int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2))
                h.update(f.read(w * (rows - rows * 12 // 100)))
        return h.hexdigest()


def fingerprint(path, text):
    """Text and page images together; a PDF neither can read falls back to its bytes."""
    body, pix = textprint(text), pageprint(path)
    if pix:
        return "page:" + hashlib.sha256(f"{body}|{pix}".encode()).hexdigest()
    if body:
        return body
    with open(path, "rb") as f:
        return "bytes:" + hashlib.sha256(f.read()).hexdigest()


def pages(path):
    r = subprocess.run(["pdfinfo", path], capture_output=True, text=True)
    m = re.search(r"^Pages:\s+(\d+)", r.stdout, re.M)
    return int(m.group(1)) if m else -1


# The stamp is appended to the PDF as an incremental update: every page gets a content stream that draws the line,
# its old bytes are left as they are, and a new cross-reference section points past them. Nothing is re-rendered,
# so links, the outline and the document's metadata survive (a pdfpages re-render dropped all three). The reader
# below knows only what that needs: the cross-reference table or stream, object streams and FlateDecode.
class _Name(str):
    pass


class _Ref(tuple):
    pass


class _Real(float):
    pass


class _Stream:
    def __init__(self, d, data):
        self.d, self.data = d, data


class _Unreadable(Exception):
    pass


_WS, _DELIM = b"\x00\t\n\x0c\r ", b"()<>[]{}/%"
_NUMRE = re.compile(rb"[+-]?(\d+\.?\d*|\.\d+)")
_REFRE = re.compile(rb"\s*(\d+)\s+(\d+)\s+R(?![^\x00\t\n\x0c\r ()<>\[\]{}/%])")


def _skip(b, i):
    while i < len(b):
        if b[i] in _WS:
            i += 1
        elif b[i] == 37:                                  # % comment to end of line
            while i < len(b) and b[i] not in b"\r\n":
                i += 1
        else:
            break
    return i


def _obj(b, i):
    """The PDF object at b[i:] and the offset after it."""
    i = _skip(b, i)
    c = b[i:i + 1]
    if b[i:i + 2] == b"<<":
        d, i = {}, i + 2
        while True:
            i = _skip(b, i)
            if b[i:i + 2] == b">>":
                return d, i + 2
            k, i = _obj(b, i)
            d[str(k)], i = _obj(b, i)
    if c == b"[":
        a, i = [], i + 1
        while True:
            i = _skip(b, i)
            if b[i:i + 1] == b"]":
                return a, i + 1
            v, i = _obj(b, i)
            a.append(v)
    if c == b"/":
        j = i + 1
        while j < len(b) and b[j] not in _WS and b[j] not in _DELIM:
            j += 1
        return _Name(b[i + 1:j].decode("latin-1")), j
    if c == b"(":
        out, depth, j = bytearray(), 1, i + 1
        while True:
            ch = b[j]
            if ch == 92:                                  # backslash: keep the escape, the string is only copied
                out += b[j:j + 2]
                j += 2
                continue
            depth += ch == 40
            depth -= ch == 41
            if depth == 0:
                return bytes(out), j + 1
            out.append(ch)
            j += 1
    if c == b"<":
        j = b.index(b">", i)
        return ("hex", b[i + 1:j]), j + 1
    m = _NUMRE.match(b, i)
    if m:
        s = m.group(0)
        if b"." not in s:
            r = _REFRE.match(b, i)
            if r:
                return _Ref((int(r.group(1)), int(r.group(2)))), r.end()
            return int(s), m.end()
        return _Real(s.decode()), m.end()
    for word, v in ((b"true", True), (b"false", False), (b"null", None)):
        if b.startswith(word, i):
            return v, i + len(word)
    raise _Unreadable(f"unexpected {b[i:i + 12]!r} at {i}")


def _ser(o):
    if isinstance(o, _Name):
        return b"/" + o.encode("latin-1")
    if isinstance(o, _Ref):
        return b"%d %d R" % o
    if isinstance(o, bool):
        return b"true" if o else b"false"
    if o is None:
        return b"null"
    if isinstance(o, int):
        return b"%d" % o
    if isinstance(o, float):
        return (repr(o) if isinstance(o, _Real) else "%.3f" % o).encode()
    if isinstance(o, bytes):
        return b"(" + o + b")"
    if isinstance(o, tuple):                              # ("hex", digits)
        return b"<" + o[1] + b">"
    if isinstance(o, list):
        return b"[" + b" ".join(_ser(v) for v in o) + b"]"
    if isinstance(o, dict):
        return b"<<" + b"".join(b"/" + k.encode("latin-1") + b" " + _ser(v) + b"\n" for k, v in o.items()) + b">>"
    raise _Unreadable(f"cannot write {type(o).__name__}")


class _PDF:
    def __init__(self, data):
        self.b, self.xref, self.trailer, self._stms = data, {}, None, {}
        m = list(re.finditer(rb"startxref\s+(\d+)", data[-2048:]))
        if not m:
            raise _Unreadable("no startxref")
        off, seen = int(m[-1].group(1)), set()
        self.last_is_stream = not data.startswith(b"xref", off)
        while off is not None and off not in seen:
            seen.add(off)
            t = self._section(off)
            if self.trailer is None:
                self.trailer = t
            if "XRefStm" in t:
                self._section(t["XRefStm"])
            off = t.get("Prev")
        if "Encrypt" in self.trailer:
            raise _Unreadable("encrypted")
        self.lastxref = int(m[-1].group(1))

    def _put(self, n, entry):
        self.xref.setdefault(n, entry)                    # newest section first, so the first entry wins

    def _section(self, off):
        b = self.b
        if b.startswith(b"xref", off):
            i = off + 4
            while True:
                i = _skip(b, i)
                if b.startswith(b"trailer", i):
                    return _obj(b, i + 7)[0]
                m = re.compile(rb"(\d+)\s+(\d+)").match(b, i)
                first, count = int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2))
                i = _skip(b, m.end())
                for k in range(count):
                    f = b[i:i + 20].split()
                    if f[2] == b"n":
                        self._put(first + k, (1, int(f[0]), int(f[1])))
                    else:
                        self._put(first + k, (0,))
                    i = _skip(b, i + 18)
        s = self._at(off)
        if not isinstance(s, _Stream) or s.d.get("Type") != "XRef":
            raise _Unreadable(f"no cross-reference at {off}")
        w, data = s.d["W"], self._decode(s)
        idx, pos = s.d.get("Index", [0, s.d["Size"]]), 0
        for first, count in zip(idx[::2], idx[1::2]):
            for k in range(count):
                f = []
                for width in w:
                    f.append(int.from_bytes(data[pos:pos + width], "big"))
                    pos += width
                typ = f[0] if w[0] else 1
                self._put(first + k, (typ, f[1], f[2]) if typ in (1, 2) else (0,))
        return s.d

    def _decode(self, s):
        f = s.d.get("Filter")
        f = f if isinstance(f, list) else [f] if f else []
        if f not in ([], ["FlateDecode"]):
            raise _Unreadable(f"filter {f}")
        data = zlib.decompress(s.data) if f else s.data
        p = s.d.get("DecodeParms") or {}
        p = p[0] if isinstance(p, list) else p
        if p.get("Predictor", 1) >= 10:                   # PNG rows, each led by its filter byte
            cols = p.get("Columns", 1) * p.get("Colors", 1) * p.get("BitsPerComponent", 8) // 8
            out, prev = bytearray(), bytearray(cols)
            for r in range(0, len(data), cols + 1):
                t, row = data[r], bytearray(data[r + 1:r + 1 + cols])
                for x in range(len(row)):
                    left = row[x - 1] if x else 0
                    up = prev[x]
                    if t == 1:
                        row[x] = (row[x] + left) & 255
                    elif t == 2:
                        row[x] = (row[x] + up) & 255
                    elif t == 3:
                        row[x] = (row[x] + (left + up) // 2) & 255
                    elif t == 4:
                        ul = prev[x - 1] if x else 0
                        pa, pb, pc = abs(up - ul), abs(left - ul), abs(left + up - 2 * ul)
                        row[x] = (row[x] + (left if pa <= pb and pa <= pc else up if pb <= pc else ul)) & 255
                out += row
                prev = row
            data = bytes(out)
        return data

    def _at(self, off):
        """The indirect object at byte offset `off`."""
        m = re.compile(rb"\s*\d+\s+\d+\s+obj").match(self.b, off)
        if not m:
            raise _Unreadable(f"no object at {off}")
        o, i = _obj(self.b, m.end())
        i = _skip(self.b, i)
        if isinstance(o, dict) and self.b.startswith(b"stream", i):
            i += 6
            i += 2 if self.b.startswith(b"\r\n", i) else 1
            n = self.get(o["Length"])
            return _Stream(o, self.b[i:i + n])
        return o

    def get(self, o):
        """o, with a reference followed."""
        if not isinstance(o, _Ref):
            return o
        e = self.xref.get(o[0], (0,))
        if e[0] == 1:
            return self._at(e[1])
        if e[0] == 2:
            if e[1] not in self._stms:
                s = self._at(self.xref[e[1]][1])
                data = self._decode(s)
                nums = [int(x) for x in data[:s.d["First"]].split()]
                self._stms[e[1]] = (data, s.d["First"], dict(zip(nums[::2], nums[1::2])))
            data, first, offs = self._stms[e[1]]
            return _obj(data, first + offs[o[0]])[0]
        return None

    def gen(self, n):
        e = self.xref.get(n, (0,))
        return e[2] if e[0] == 1 else 0

    def pages(self, node=None, inherit=None):
        """(ref, page dict, inherited Resources/MediaBox/CropBox) for every page in order."""
        if node is None:
            node = self.get(self.get(self.trailer["Root"])["Pages"])
        inherit = dict(inherit or {})
        for k in ("Resources", "MediaBox", "CropBox"):
            if k in node:
                inherit[k] = node[k]
        for kid in node.get("Kids", []):
            d = self.get(kid)
            if d.get("Type") == "Pages" or "Kids" in d:
                yield from self.pages(d, inherit)
            else:
                yield kid, d, inherit


def overlay(src, dst, text):
    """src with `text` small and grey at the bottom left of every page, appended as an incremental update, to dst."""
    with open(src, "rb") as f:
        data = f.read()
    pdf = _PDF(data)
    size = pdf.trailer["Size"]
    new, nums = [], {}

    def add(o):
        new.append((len(new) + size, 0, o))
        return _Ref((new[-1][0], 0))

    font = add({"Type": _Name("Font"), "Subtype": _Name("Type1"), "BaseFont": _Name("Helvetica"),
                "Encoding": _Name("WinAnsiEncoding")})
    push = add(_Stream({}, b"q\n"))
    lit = text.encode("cp1252").replace(b"\\", b"\\\\").replace(b"(", b"\\(").replace(b")", b"\\)")
    for ref, page, inh in list(pdf.pages()):
        if not isinstance(ref, _Ref):
            raise _Unreadable("a page that is not an indirect object")
        box = [float(pdf.get(v)) for v in pdf.get(page.get("CropBox") or inh.get("CropBox") or page.get("MediaBox")
                                                    or inh.get("MediaBox"))]
        at = (min(box[0], box[2]) + 30, min(box[1], box[3]) + 20)
        if at not in nums:
            nums[at] = add(_Stream({}, b"Q q BT /CCDocsStamp 7 Tf 0.5 g %.2f %.2f Td (%s) Tj ET Q\n"
                                   % (at[0], at[1], lit)))
        res = dict(pdf.get(page.get("Resources", inh.get("Resources"))) or {})
        res["Font"] = dict(pdf.get(res.get("Font")) or {}, CCDocsStamp=font)
        c = page.get("Contents")
        c = pdf.get(c) if isinstance(c, _Ref) and not isinstance(pdf.get(c), _Stream) else c
        c = c if isinstance(c, list) else [] if c is None else [c]
        new.append((ref[0], ref[1], dict(page, Resources=res, Contents=[push] + c + [nums[at]])))
    out = bytearray(data if data.endswith(b"\n") else data + b"\n")
    offs = {}
    for n, g, o in new:
        offs[n] = (len(out), g)
        out += b"%d %d obj\n" % (n, g)
        if isinstance(o, _Stream):
            out += _ser(dict(o.d, Length=len(o.data))) + b"\nstream\n" + o.data + b"\nendstream"
        else:
            out += _ser(o)
        out += b"\nendobj\n"
    t = {k: pdf.trailer[k] for k in ("Root", "Info", "ID") if k in pdf.trailer}
    t.update(Size=max(offs) + 1, Prev=pdf.lastxref)
    if pdf.last_is_stream:
        n = t["Size"]
        t["Size"] = n + 1
        offs[n] = (len(out), 0)
        rows = sorted(offs)
        idx = []
        for k in rows:
            if idx and idx[-2] + idx[-1] == k:
                idx[-1] += 1
            else:
                idx += [k, 1]
        body = b"".join(b"\x01" + offs[k][0].to_bytes(4, "big") + offs[k][1].to_bytes(2, "big") for k in rows)
        xref = len(out)
        out += b"%d 0 obj\n" % n + _ser(dict(t, Type=_Name("XRef"), W=[1, 4, 2], Index=idx, Length=len(body)))
        out += b"\nstream\n" + body + b"\nendstream\nendobj\n"
    else:
        xref = len(out)
        out += b"xref\n"
        for k in sorted(offs):
            out += b"%d 1\n%010d %05d n\r\n" % (k, offs[k][0], offs[k][1])
        out += b"trailer\n" + _ser(t) + b"\n"
    out += b"startxref\n%d\n%%%%EOF\n" % xref
    with open(dst, "wb") as f:
        f.write(out)


def stamp(src, dst, text):
    """Every page of src with `text` small and grey at the bottom left, written to dst. The line is appended to the
    PDF (overlay above), so its links, outline and metadata survive; a PDF that reader cannot follow (encrypted, or
    a filter it does not know) is re-rendered through pdfpages instead, which loses them, and says so on stderr."""
    try:
        overlay(src, dst, text)
        if pages(dst) == pages(src) and text in pdftext(dst):
            return
        why = "the appended stamp did not read back"
    except (_Unreadable, Refused, KeyError, ValueError, IndexError, TypeError, AttributeError, zlib.error) as e:
        why = str(e) or type(e).__name__
    print(f"cc-docs: {src}: stamping by re-rendering its pages ({why}); its links and outline are lost",
          file=sys.stderr)
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="cc-docs-") as t:
        shutil.copy(src, os.path.join(t, "in.pdf"))
        tex = text.replace("·", r"\textperiodcentered{}")
        with open(os.path.join(t, "s.tex"), "w") as f:
            f.write("\\documentclass{article}\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\\usepackage{pdfpages}\\usepackage{xcolor}\n"
                    "\\begin{document}\\includepdf[pages=-,fitpaper,picturecommand={\\put(30,20){\\fontsize{7}{8}"
                    "\\selectfont\\sffamily\\color[gray]{0.5}" + tex + "}}]{in.pdf}\\end{document}\n")
        r = subprocess.run(["pdflatex", "-interaction=batchmode", "-halt-on-error", "s.tex"], cwd=t,
                           capture_output=True, text=True)
        out = os.path.join(t, "s.pdf")
        if r.returncode != 0 or not os.path.isfile(out) or pages(out) != pages(src):
            raise Refused(f"{src}: the stamp overlay failed (pdflatex exit {r.returncode}); nothing filed")
        shutil.copy(out, dst)


# ── the source ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
TEXREF = re.compile(r"\\(input|include|subfile|includegraphics|includesvg|includepdf|lstinputlisting|bibliography|"
                    r"addbibresource|bibliographystyle|usepackage|RequirePackage|documentclass|LoadClass|graphicspath)"
                    r"\*?\s*(?:\[[^\]]*\]\s*)*\{((?:[^{}]|\{[^{}]*\})*)\}|\\input\s+([^\s{}\\%]+)")
EXTS = {"input": (".tex", ""), "include": (".tex",), "subfile": (".tex", ""), "lstinputlisting": ("",),
        "includegraphics": ("", ".pdf", ".png", ".jpg", ".jpeg", ".eps"), "includesvg": (".svg", ""),
        "includepdf": ("", ".pdf"), "bibliography": (".bib",), "addbibresource": ("",), "bibliographystyle": (".bst",),
        "usepackage": (".sty",), "RequirePackage": (".sty",), "documentclass": (".cls",), "LoadClass": (".cls",)}
PKGCMDS = ("usepackage", "RequirePackage", "documentclass", "LoadClass")
PICEXTS = (".pdf", ".png", ".jpg", ".jpeg", ".eps")   # what a macro's argument is tried as: graphicx's own order
CWDCMDS = ("input", "include", "subfile", "includegraphics", "includesvg", "includepdf", "lstinputlisting")
CWD = "_cwd"              # where a file found from a directory above the .tex is packed; on texinputs
STYLECMDS = PKGCMDS + ("input",)
PIN = re.compile(r"^\s*%\s*!\s*TEX\s+(?:TS-)?program\s*=\s*([A-Za-z]+)", re.I)
ENGINES = ("pdflatex", "lualatex", "xelatex")
OTHER = {"pdflatex": "lualatex", "lualatex": "pdflatex"}   # the one retry an unpinned source gets
MANIFEST = ".source.json"
SRC_CAP = 48 << 20        # the most source kept for one revision, in bytes: a file past it is left out and listed
SRC_FILES = 400
CHECK_WAIT = 120          # seconds one compile check may take


def conf(key, default=""):
    """A cc-config key, the environment winning: this repo's own cc-config first (a landing's gates run on a bare
    PATH with no ~/bin shim), else the one on PATH."""
    here = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "cc-config")
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([here if os.access(here, os.X_OK) else "cc-config", "get", key, default],
                           capture_output=True, text=True)
    except OSError:
        return default
    return r.stdout.strip() if r.returncode == 0 else default


def style_trees():
    """DOCS_TEX_TREES as [(root, sub)]: each entry ROOT:SUB is a house style a maker puts on TEXINPUTS as ROOT/SUB//."""
    out = []
    for e in conf("DOCS_TEX_TREES").split():
        root, _, sub = e.partition(":")
        root, sub = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(root)), sub.strip("/")
        if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(root, sub)):
            out.append((root, sub))
    return out


class Found(list):
    """tex_sources' [(path, name in the tarball)], with what the manifest needs: main (the .tex's name), pin (the
    engine a `% !TEX program` line names, else None), unicode (fontspec or unicode-math is loaded) and texinputs."""
    main = pin = None
    unicode = False

    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.texinputs = []


def tex_sources(tex, trees=None, styles=None):
    """Found for a LaTeX build: the .tex and every local file it pulls in, read the way LaTeX finds them — beside
    the .tex (and its \\graphicspath), then in a DOCS_TEX_TREES style tree (packed under _style/, with every font
    of that tree), then a package or class through kpsewhich when that lands under ~ (packed at the tarball's root,
    where TeX finds it), never one of TeX's own. With trees (a member's filing) a file whose real path is outside
    them is not read at all, bar the box's own style trees (DOCS_TEX_TREES, which a member cannot name or write),
    and kpsewhich is not asked."""
    base = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(tex))
    if styles is None:
        styles = style_trees()
    walked, used = {}, []
    # a member's document on the house style (901-0001 uses housestyle) compiles with it, so the box's own
    # style roots are read for it too; nothing else outside the member's trees is
    allowed = readable(trees, styles)

    def in_style(name, exts):
        for root, sub in styles:
            if (root, sub) not in walked:
                walked[(root, sub)] = sorted(os.path.join(dp, x) for dp, _, fn in os.walk(os.path.join(root, sub))
                                             for x in fn)
            for e in exts:
                want = "/" + os.path.normpath(name + e).lstrip("/")
                hit = next((p for p in walked[(root, sub)] if p.endswith(want)), None)
                if hit:
                    return hit, root, sub
        return None
    def from_cwd(nm, exts):
        """A path a build that ran from a directory above the .tex's resolves (`reports/schematic.pdf` in
        reports/design_doc/x.tex, built from the board's root): the nearest such directory under ~ that has it.
        -> (path, _cwd/<nm>), where TEXINPUTS finds it, or None."""
        if nm.startswith("/") or ".." in nm.split("/"):
            return None
        d = os.path.dirname(base)
        while d.startswith(HOME + "/"):
            for e in exts:
                p = os.path.join(d, nm + e)
                if os.path.isfile(p):
                    return p, CWD + "/" + os.path.normpath(nm + e)
            d = os.path.dirname(d)
        return None
    todo, seen, out, gpath = [(os.path.abspath(tex), None)], set(), Found(), [""]
    while todo and len(out) < SRC_FILES:
        f, name = todo.pop(0)
        real = os.path.realpath(f)
        if real in seen or not os.path.isfile(real) or (allowed is not None and not within(real, allowed)):
            continue
        seen.add(real)
        name = name or (os.path.relpath(f, base) if f.startswith(base + "/") else
                        "_ext/" + (os.path.relpath(f, HOME) if f.startswith(HOME + "/") else f.lstrip("/")))
        out.append((real, name))
        if not f.endswith((".tex", ".sty", ".cls")):
            continue
        try:
            raw = open(real, errors="replace").read()
        except OSError:
            continue
        if out.main is None:
            out.main = name
            pin = next((m.group(1).lower() for ln in raw.splitlines()[:20] for m in [PIN.match(ln)] if m), None)
            out.pin = pin if pin in ENGINES else None
        body = re.sub(r"(?<!\\)%.*", "", raw)
        for m in TEXREF.finditer(body):
            cmd, arg = (m.group(1), m.group(2)) if m.group(1) else ("input", m.group(3))
            if cmd == "graphicspath":
                gpath += re.findall(r"\{([^{}]*)\}", arg)
                continue
            for nm in (x.strip() for x in arg.split(",") if x.strip()):
                if cmd in ("usepackage", "RequirePackage") and nm in ("fontspec", "unicode-math"):
                    out.unicode = True
                dirs = gpath if cmd in ("includegraphics", "includesvg") else [""]
                hit = next((p for d in dirs for e in EXTS[cmd] for p in [os.path.normpath(os.path.join(base, d, nm + e))]
                            if os.path.isfile(p)), None)
                if hit:
                    todo.append((hit, None))
                    continue
                up = from_cwd(nm, EXTS[cmd]) if cmd in CWDCMDS else None
                if up:
                    todo.append(up)
                    if CWD not in out.texinputs:
                        out.texinputs.append(CWD)
                    continue
                s = in_style(nm, EXTS[cmd]) if styles and cmd in STYLECMDS else None
                if s:
                    todo.append((s[0], "_style/" + os.path.relpath(s[0], s[1])))
                    if "_style/" + s[2] not in out.texinputs:
                        out.texinputs.append("_style/" + s[2])
                    if s[1] not in used:
                        used.append(s[1])
                    continue
                if cmd in PKGCMDS and trees is None:
                    try:
                        k = subprocess.run(["kpsewhich", nm + EXTS[cmd][0]], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()
                    except OSError:
                        k = ""
                    if k.startswith(HOME + "/") and os.path.isfile(k):
                        todo.append((k, os.path.basename(k)))
        # fontspec's Path= (`\\setmainfont{SourceSerif4}[Path=fonts/, …]`): every font in that folder, which
        # UprightFont=*-Regular and the like pick from
        for d in re.findall(r"\bPath\s*=\s*\{?([^,\]\s{}]+)", body):
            fd = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(base, d))
            if not d.startswith("/") and os.path.isdir(fd):
                todo += [(os.path.join(fd, x), None) for x in sorted(os.listdir(fd))
                         if x.lower().endswith((".otf", ".ttf")) and os.path.isfile(os.path.join(fd, x))]
        if f.endswith(".tex"):
            # a figure named through a macro of the document or its style (\hsdiagram{figures/x}): any argument
            # that is a picture beside the .tex, in its \graphicspath or in a folder beside it (a macro that puts
            # `figures/` in front itself), under the extensions TeX tries
            try:
                subs = sorted(x + "/" for x in os.listdir(base) if not x.startswith(".")
                              and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(base, x)))
            except OSError:
                subs = []
            for m in re.finditer(r"\{([A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_./+-]*)\}", body):
                nm = m.group(1)
                if ".." in nm.split("/"):
                    continue
                exts = ("",) * nm.lower().endswith(PICEXTS) + PICEXTS
                hit = next((p for d in gpath + subs for e in exts for p in [os.path.normpath(os.path.join(base, d, nm + e))]
                            if p.startswith(base + "/") and os.path.isfile(p)), None)
                if hit:
                    todo.append((hit, None))
    reroot(out, base)
    for root in used:   # the house style finds its fonts beside itself, at <its dir>/../../assets/fonts/
        for dp, _, fn in sorted(os.walk(root)):
            for x in sorted(fn):
                p = os.path.join(dp, x)
                if x.lower().endswith((".otf", ".ttf")) and os.path.realpath(p) not in seen and os.path.isfile(p):
                    seen.add(os.path.realpath(p))
                    out.append((os.path.realpath(p), "_style/" + os.path.relpath(p, root)))
    return out


def reroot(out, base):
    """A .tex reaching up (`\\input{../ResumeInclude/x.tex}`) is kept with the tree it reaches: every _ext/ file
    under ~ is packed at its path under the nearest folder holding it and the .tex (never ~ itself), and the .tex's
    own files (and the packages kpsewhich found, beside it) in their folder under that one, the main with them. The
    editor compiles such a main from its own folder, where `..` reaches the root again. _style/ and _cwd/ stay put."""
    ext = [HOME + "/" + nm[len("_ext/"):] for _, nm in out if nm.startswith("_ext/")]
    ext = [x for x in ext if os.path.exists(x)]
    if not ext or not base.startswith(HOME + "/"):
        return
    root = os.path.commonpath([base] + [os.path.dirname(x) for x in ext])
    if root == base or not root.startswith(HOME + "/"):
        return
    pre = os.path.relpath(base, root)
    for i, (real, nm) in enumerate(out):
        if nm.startswith("_ext/"):
            lex = HOME + "/" + nm[len("_ext/"):]
            if lex in ext:
                out[i] = (real, os.path.relpath(lex, root))
        elif not nm.startswith(("_style/", CWD + "/")):
            out[i] = (real, pre + "/" + nm)
    if out.main:
        out.main = pre + "/" + out.main


def find_sources(a, pdf):
    """What `file` keeps as a revision's source: --latex, else a --source that is a .tex, else a .tex of the PDF's
    own name beside it (a LaTeX build), each with what it includes; else the --source file itself; else nothing."""
    trees = getattr(a, "trees", None)
    source = getattr(a, "srcpath", None) or a.source     # a member's Slack-files path, as the host sees it
    tex = getattr(a, "latex", None)
    if not tex and source and source.endswith(".tex"):
        tex = source
    if not tex and not getattr(a, "origin", None):
        sib = os.path.splitext(pdf)[0] + ".tex"
        tex = sib if os.path.isfile(sib) else None
    if tex:
        return tex_sources(tex, trees)
    if source and os.path.isfile(source) and (trees is None or within(os.path.realpath(source), trees)):
        return [(os.path.abspath(source), os.path.basename(source))]
    return []


def pack(files, dst, trees=None, extra=()):
    """files as one gzip tarball at dst, the same bytes for the same files (sorted, mtime 0, no owner), with extra
    [(name, bytes)] beside them (the manifest). -> (names kept, names left out past SRC_CAP), extra not among them.
    With trees each file is read from one fd whose own path must be inside them (member_pdf's reasoning), so a link
    swapped in after tex_sources looked cannot pull a host file in (the box's own style roots are allowed too)."""
    import gzip
    import io
    import tarfile
    kept, left, total = [], [], 0
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
    items = [(name, path, None) for path, name in files] + [(name, None, data) for name, data in extra]
    with open(dst + ".part", "wb") as raw, gzip.GzipFile(filename="", mode="wb", fileobj=raw, mtime=0) as gz, \
            tarfile.open(fileobj=gz, mode="w", format=tarfile.PAX_FORMAT) as tar:
        for name, path, data in sorted(items, key=lambda x: x[0]):
            if path is not None:
                try:
                    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
                except OSError:
                    continue
                with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as f:
                    if trees is not None and not within(os.readlink(f"/proc/self/fd/{fd}"), readable(trees)):
                        continue
                    data = f.read(SRC_CAP + 1)
                if total + len(data) > SRC_CAP:
                    left.append(name)
                    continue
                total += len(data)
                kept.append(name)
            ti = tarfile.TarInfo(name)
            ti.size, ti.mode, ti.mtime = len(data), 0o644, 0
            tar.addfile(ti, io.BytesIO(data))
    os.chmod(dst + ".part", 0o444)
    os.replace(dst + ".part", dst)
    return kept, left


def manifest(found, engine):
    m = {"main": found.main, "engine": engine}
    if found.texinputs:
        m["texinputs"] = list(found.texinputs)
    return (json.dumps(m, indent=1, sort_keys=True) + "\n").encode()


def utcnow():
    return datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def run_check(cmd, tarball, engine=None):
    """DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK on one tarball. -> (its verdict, whether it ran): exit 0 and ok is a pass, exit 1 a
    failure with its errors, anything else (or no JSON, or past CHECK_WAIT) a check that could not run, said with
    the verdict's own first message when it printed one."""
    argv = shlex.split(cmd) + (["--engine", engine] if engine else []) + [tarball]
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=CHECK_WAIT, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        return {"ok": False, "errors": [{"message": f"{e}"[:300]}]}, False
    try:
        v = json.loads(r.stdout)
    except ValueError:
        try:
            v = json.loads((r.stdout.strip().splitlines() or [""])[-1])
        except ValueError:
            v = None
    if r.returncode not in (0, 1) or not isinstance(v, dict):
        said = isinstance(v, dict) and next((e.get("message") for e in v.get("errors") or []
                                             if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("message")), None)
        why = said or (r.stderr.strip().splitlines() or [f"exit {r.returncode}, no verdict"])[-1]
        return {"ok": False, "errors": [{"message": f"exit {r.returncode}: {why}"[:300]}]}, False
    v["ok"] = r.returncode == 0 and v.get("ok") is True
    return v, True


def first_error(v, ran=True):
    e = next((x for x in v.get("errors") or [] if isinstance(x, dict)), {})
    msg = str(e.get("message") or "no error given")[:300]
    return f"{e.get('path') or '?'}:{e.get('line') or '?'}: {msg}" if ran else msg


def sha_of(path):
    h = hashlib.sha256()
    with open(path, "rb") as f:
        for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(1 << 20), b""):
            h.update(chunk)
    return h.hexdigest()


def read_checks():
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(ROOT, "checks.json")) as f:
            c = json.load(f)
        return c if isinstance(c, dict) else {}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


def update_checks(fn):
    """checks.json changed by fn, under a lock of its own and replaced whole."""
    os.makedirs(ROOT, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(ROOT, ".checks.lock"), "w") as lf:
        fcntl.flock(lf, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        c = read_checks()
        fn(c)
        fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=ROOT, prefix=".checks.")
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
            json.dump(c, f, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
            f.write("\n")
        os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(ROOT, "checks.json"))


def record_passes(passes):
    if passes:
        update_checks(lambda c: c.setdefault("passes", {}).update(passes))


class Staged:
    """A revision's source packed in a scratch dir under the register and checked, waiting for commit()."""
    def __init__(self):
        os.makedirs(ROOT, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
        self.dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=ROOT, prefix=".source.")
        self.tar = os.path.join(self.dir, "source.tar.gz")
        self.fields = {}

    def commit(self, proj, full):
        """Into sources/PPP/<full>.tar.gz, replacing what was there. -> the fields its revision records."""
        rel = os.path.join("sources", proj, f"{full}.tar.gz")
        os.makedirs(os.path.join(ROOT, "sources", proj), exist_ok=True)
        os.replace(self.tar, os.path.join(ROOT, rel))
        if self.fields.get("source_checked"):
            record_passes({sha_of(os.path.join(ROOT, rel)): {"at": self.fields["source_checked"],
                                                              "engine": self.fields["source_engine"]}})
        return dict(self.fields, sources=rel)

    def close(self):
        shutil.rmtree(self.dir, ignore_errors=True)


def stage_sources(files, full, trees=None):
    """Pack a revision's source and, for a LaTeX one, run DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK on it, once more with the other engine
    when the first fails and no `% !TEX program` pinned it. -> (Staged, "") to keep, or (None, why not)."""
    if not files:
        return None, "nothing to keep"
    try:
        st = Staged()
    except OSError as e:
        print(f"cc-docs: the source of {full} was not kept: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return None, str(e)
    try:
        main = getattr(files, "main", None)
        cmd = conf("DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK") if main else ""
        engine = (files.pin or ("lualatex" if files.unicode else "pdflatex")) if main else None
        tries = [engine] + ([OTHER[engine]] if main and not files.pin and engine in OTHER and cmd else [])
        failed = None
        for e in tries:
            kept, left = pack(files, st.tar, trees, [(MANIFEST, manifest(files, e))] if main else ())
            st.fields = {"source_files": kept}
            if main:
                st.fields.update(source_main=main, source_engine=e)
            if not cmd:
                failed = None
                break
            v, ran = run_check(cmd, st.tar, e)
            if v["ok"]:
                st.fields["source_checked"] = utcnow()
                failed = None
                break
            failed = failed or (v, ran)
            if not ran:
                break
        if failed:
            v, ran = failed
            why = first_error(v, ran)
            print(f"cc-docs: {full}: source not kept, " + ("it does not compile: " if ran else
                  "the compile check could not run: ") + why, file=sys.stderr)
            st.close()
            return None, ("does not compile: " if ran else "check could not run: ") + why
        if left:
            print(f"cc-docs: {full}: {len(left)} source file(s) left out past {SRC_CAP >> 20} MiB: "
                  f"{', '.join(left[:5])}", file=sys.stderr)
        if not kept:
            st.close()
            return None, "no file could be read"
        return st, ""
    except OSError as e:
        print(f"cc-docs: the source of {full} was not kept: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        st.close()
        return None, str(e)


def keep_sources(files, proj, full, trees=None):
    """Pack (and check) a revision's source into sources/PPP/<full>.tar.gz. -> the fields its revision records,
    or {}."""
    st, _ = stage_sources(files, full, trees)
    if not st:
        return {}
    try:
        return st.commit(proj, full)
    finally:
        st.close()


# ── who filed it ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def _cwds():
    """This process's cwd, then each ancestor's: a maker's build runs in a scratch dir, its session in the tree."""
    out, pid = [os.getcwd()], os.getppid()
    for _ in range(16):
        try:
            out.append(os.readlink(f"/proc/{pid}/cwd"))
            pid = int(open(f"/proc/{pid}/stat").read().rsplit(")", 1)[1].split()[1])
        except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
            break
        if pid <= 1:
            break
    return out


def filer():
    """{repo, session, target, channel, thread, alias} of the session filing, as far as the box can tell: a track
    worktree's .cc/track (its thread from cc-slack's track-threads.json), an orch's CC_SLACK_ALIAS (its channel from
    orchs.json), else ~/dev/<repo> (the repo's channel). Keys it cannot tell are left out."""
    slack = os.environ.get("CC_SLACK_DIR") or os.path.join(HOME, ".cc", "slack")

    def table(name):
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(slack, name)) as f:
                return json.load(f)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            return {}
    out, dev = {}, os.path.join(HOME, "dev") + "/"
    for c in _cwds():
        x = os.path.realpath(c)
        while x not in ("/", "") and "target" not in out:
            try:
                repo, track = (open(os.path.join(x, ".cc", "track")).read().split() + ["", ""])[:2]
            except OSError:
                repo = track = ""
            if repo and track:
                out.update(repo=repo, session=track, target=f"{repo}/{track}")
                t = table("track-threads.json").get(out["target"]) or {}
                if t.get("chat") and t.get("ts"):
                    out.update(channel=t["chat"], thread=t["ts"])
            x = os.path.dirname(x)
        if "target" not in out and os.path.realpath(c).startswith(dev):
            out.setdefault("repo", os.path.realpath(c)[len(dev):].split("/")[0])
        if "target" in out:
            break
    alias = os.environ.get("CC_SLACK_ALIAS")
    if alias and "target" not in out:
        out.update(alias=alias, session=alias)
        for chan, o in table("orchs.json").items():
            if isinstance(o, dict) and o.get("alias") == alias and not o.get("archived") and not o.get("superseded_by") \
                    and (not out.get("repo") or o.get("target") == out["repo"]):
                out.update(channel=chan, repo=o.get("target"), target=o.get("target"))
                break
    if out.get("repo") and "target" not in out:
        out["target"] = out["repo"]
    if out.get("target") and "channel" not in out:
        ch = table("channels.json").get(out["target"])
        if isinstance(ch, str):
            out["channel"] = ch
    return {k: v for k, v in out.items() if v}


# ── feedback from the library site ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def feedback_path():
    return os.path.join(ROOT, "feedback.json")


def answer_feedback(num, rev, old=()):
    """A new revision answers its document's open feedback: each item delivered (or new) for `num`, or for a number
    it was moved from (`old`), becomes done, reply "answered by rev <rev>", unsynced until the box's poller tells the
    site. Called under Lock. -> count."""
    try:
        with open(feedback_path()) as f:
            fb = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return 0
    n = 0
    for it in fb.get("items", {}).values():
        doc = str(it.get("number") or "")
        if doc.count("-") == 2:
            doc = doc.rsplit("-", 1)[0]
        if (doc == num or doc in old) and it.get("status") in ("new", "delivered"):
            it.update(status="done", reply=f"answered by rev {rev}", synced=False,
                      done_at=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"))
            n += 1
    if n:
        fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=ROOT, prefix=".feedback.")
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
            json.dump(fb, f, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
            f.write("\n")
        os.replace(tmp, feedback_path())
    return n


# ── commands ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def plan(reg, a):
    """-> (proj, docnum, doc-or-None, next letter). Creates the project in reg (the caller decides to save)."""
    proj = find_project(reg, a.project)
    if not proj:
        if re.fullmatch(r"\d{3}", a.project):
            raise Refused(f"no project {a.project}: create it by name with `cc-docs project <name> --number {a.project}`")
        proj = make_project(reg, a.project, None, a.kind, a.member)
    source = os.path.abspath(a.source) if a.source else None
    num = match_doc(reg, proj, a.title, source)
    d = reg["documents"].get(num) if num else None
    return proj, num or next_doc(reg, proj), d, letter(len(d["revisions"]) + len(d.get("retired_revs", ())) if d else 0)


def cmd_file(a):
    src = os.path.abspath(a.pdf)
    shown = getattr(a, "origin", None) or a.pdf   # a member's PDF is filed from the host's copy; its own path is the one named
    if not os.path.isfile(src):
        raise Refused(f"{shown}: no such file")
    date = datetime.date.fromisoformat(a.date) if a.date else datetime.date.today()
    describes, cost = check_describes(a.describes), parse_cost(a.cost)
    text = pdftext(src)
    fp = fingerprint(src, text)
    sources = find_sources(a, src)
    with Lock():   # a first look, so an unchanged or refused build runs no compile check
        reg = load()
        proj, num, d, rev = plan(reg, a)
        fresh = not (d and current(d) and current(d)["fingerprint"] in (fp, textprint(text)))
        # an unchanged rebuild with --source keeps a source for the current revision when it has none
        full = f"{num}-{rev}" if fresh else f"{num}-{current(d)['rev']}"
        want = fresh or bool(a.source and "sources" not in current(d))
        if fresh:
            carried = set(m.group(0).split()[0] for m in STAMP.finditer(text))
            if carried - {f"{num}-{rev}"}:
                raise Refused(f"{shown} already carries {', '.join(sorted(carried - {f'{num}-{rev}'}))}, but it would "
                              f"be filed as {num}-{rev}; rebuild it with `cc-docs number`")
    # the check compiles for up to minutes, so it runs outside the register's lock, on a tarball not yet in place
    staged = stage_sources(sources, full, getattr(a, "trees", None))[0] if sources and want else None
    # a supporting file that is missing or over a cap refuses the whole call before anything is filed
    extra = StagedFiles()
    try:
        extra = stage_attachments(getattr(a, "attach", None))
        return file_locked(a, src, shown, date, describes, cost, text, fp, staged, extra)
    finally:
        extra.close()
        if staged:
            staged.close()


def file_locked(a, src, shown, date, describes, cost, text, fp, staged, extra=()):
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        proj, num, d, rev = plan(reg, a)
        # brief: "a changed finished version = next letter, unchanged content = no new letter"
        # a revision filed before page images were hashed carries a text-only print: that still counts as unchanged
        if d and current(d) and current(d)["fingerprint"] in (fp, textprint(text)):
            cur = current(d)
            # an unchanged build's supporting files go on the revision it matches, the same way `attach` puts them
            lst, said = merge_attachments(cur.get("attachments") or [], extra, False, f"{num}-{cur['rev']}")
            if extra:
                check_attachments(reg, num, cur["rev"], lst)
            print(f"{num}-{cur['rev']}\t{os.path.join(ROOT, cur['file'])}\tunchanged, nothing filed")
            # brief: "a --source on an unchanged rebuild is how a session attaches a .tex found after filing"
            recorded = []
            if a.source:
                if not d.get("source") or not os.path.exists(d["source"]):
                    d["source"] = os.path.abspath(a.source)
                    recorded.append(f"source {d['source']}")
                if "sources" not in cur and staged:
                    got = staged.commit(proj, f"{num}-{cur['rev']}")
                    if got:
                        cur.update(got)
                        recorded.append(f"sources {got['sources']}")
            if any(w != "unchanged" for _, w in said):
                extra.commit()
                cur["attachments"] = lst
                recorded.append("supporting files " + ", ".join(n for n, w in said if w != "unchanged"))
            if recorded:
                save(reg)
                write_views(reg, set(d["visibility"]) - {"owner"})
                print(f"cc-docs: {num}-{cur['rev']}: recorded {' and '.join(recorded)}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 0
        full = f"{num}-{rev}"
        carried = set(m.group(0).split()[0] for m in STAMP.finditer(text))
        if carried - {full}:
            raise Refused(f"{shown} already carries {', '.join(sorted(carried - {full}))}, but it would be filed as "
                          f"{full}; rebuild it with `cc-docs number`")
        # brief: "A later revision doesn't silently drop a revision's files"
        lst = merge_attachments(carry_attachments(current(d) if d else None, describes, extra, full), extra, False,
                                full)[0]
        check_attachments(reg, num, rev, lst)
        nostamp = a.no_stamp or bool(d and d.get("stamp") is False)
        rel = os.path.join("files", proj, f"{full}_{slugify(a.title)}.pdf")
        dst = os.path.join(ROOT, rel)
        if os.path.exists(dst):
            raise Refused(f"{dst} exists; a filed revision is never rewritten")
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
        tmp = dst + ".part"
        if nostamp:
            how = "none"
            shutil.copy(src, tmp)
        elif full in carried:
            how = "carried"
            shutil.copy(src, tmp)
        else:
            how = "overlay"
            stamp(src, tmp, " · ".join([full] + ([describes] if describes else []) + [stampdate(date)]))
        os.chmod(tmp, 0o444)
        os.replace(tmp, dst)
        with open(dst, "rb") as f:
            sha = hashlib.sha256(f.read()).hexdigest()
        if not d:
            pd = reg["projects"][proj]
            d = reg["documents"][num] = {
                "number": num, "project": proj, "title": a.title, "source": os.path.abspath(a.source) if a.source else None,
                "visibility": ["owner"] + ([pd["workspace"]] if pd.get("workspace") else []), "member": pd.get("member"),
                "starred_by": [], "stamp": not nostamp, "revisions": []}
        d["title"] = a.title
        if a.source and (not d.get("source") or not os.path.exists(d["source"])):
            d["source"] = os.path.abspath(a.source)
        d["revisions"].append({"rev": rev, "file": rel, "date": date.isoformat(), "from": getattr(a, "origin", None) or src, "fingerprint": fp,
                               "sha256": sha, "stamped": how, "pages": pages(dst), "bytes": os.path.getsize(dst),
                               "filed_at": datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")})
        who = getattr(a, "filer", None)
        who = filer() if who is None else who
        for k, v in (("note", (a.note or "").strip() or None), ("describes", describes), ("cost", cost),
                     ("filer", who)):
            if v:
                d["revisions"][-1][k] = v
        if lst:
            extra.commit()
            d["revisions"][-1]["attachments"] = lst
        if staged:
            try:
                d["revisions"][-1].update(staged.commit(proj, full))
            except OSError as e:
                print(f"cc-docs: the source of {full} was not kept: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        save(reg)
        write_views(reg, set(d["visibility"]) - {"owner"})
        # brief: "When cc-docs files a new revision of a document with open feedback, mark those done"
        answered = answer_feedback(num, rev, d.get("moved_from", ()))
    print(f"{full}\t{dst}\tfiled", flush=True)   # first: a maker that folds stderr in reads its first line
    if answered:
        print(f"cc-docs: {full} answers {answered} feedback item(s) on {num}; the library poller tells the site",
              file=sys.stderr)
    spawn_check()
    return 0


# ── supporting files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ATTACH_FILE_CAP = 25 << 20      # Cloudflare Pages serves no file over 25 MiB, and the site is served from Pages
ATTACH_REV_CAP = 100            # files on one revision
ATTACH_TOTAL_CAP = 1 << 30      # every supporting file the register names, once each: the mirror's GitHub repo
ATTACH_NAME = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9 ._+()-]{0,119}$")


class StagedFiles(list):
    """Supporting files read once, each copied aside under attachments/ while it is hashed, so what is recorded is
    what was read. commit() moves each into its blob; close() drops what was never committed."""

    def commit(self):
        for x in self:
            dst = os.path.join(ROOT, x["blob"])
            if os.path.exists(dst):
                os.unlink(x.pop("tmp"))
            else:
                os.replace(x.pop("tmp"), dst)

    def close(self):
        for x in self:
            if x.get("tmp") and os.path.exists(x["tmp"]):
                os.unlink(x["tmp"])


def stage_attachments(paths):
    """-> StagedFiles of the supporting files named, or Refused saying which one and why, nothing kept."""
    staged = StagedFiles()
    try:
        for p in paths or ():
            name = os.path.basename(p.rstrip("/"))
            if os.path.isdir(p):
                raise Refused(f"{p} is a directory: name its files (`{p.rstrip('/')}/*`) or zip it")
            if not os.path.isfile(p):
                raise Refused(f"{p}: no such file")
            if not ATTACH_NAME.match(name):
                raise Refused(f"{p}: a supporting file's name is letters, digits, space and ._+()- (at most 120, "
                              "not starting with a dot); rename it")
            if any(x["name"] == name for x in staged):
                raise Refused(f"two supporting files are named {name}")
            os.makedirs(os.path.join(ROOT, "attachments"), mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
            h, crc, size = hashlib.sha256(), 0, 0
            fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=os.path.join(ROOT, "attachments"), prefix=".part.")
            staged.append({"name": name, "tmp": tmp})
            with open(p, "rb") as f, os.fdopen(fd, "wb") as out:
                while True:
                    b = f.read(1 << 20)
                    if not b:
                        break
                    size += len(b)
                    if size > ATTACH_FILE_CAP:
                        # brief: "refuse over a cap and say why, rather than truncating"
                        raise Refused(f"{p} is over {ATTACH_FILE_CAP >> 20} MiB, the largest file the library's host "
                                      "(Cloudflare Pages) serves; split it or leave it out")
                    h.update(b)
                    crc = zlib.crc32(b, crc)
                    out.write(b)
            os.chmod(tmp, 0o444)
            sha = h.hexdigest()
            os.makedirs(os.path.join(ROOT, "attachments", sha[:2]), mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
            staged[-1].update({"blob": f"attachments/{sha[:2]}/{sha}", "bytes": size, "sha256": sha, "crc32": crc,
                               "added": utcnow()})
    except BaseException:
        staged.close()
        raise
    return staged


def merge_attachments(have, new, replace, full):
    """have with new added: a name already there with the same bytes stays as it is; with other bytes it is refused
    unless replace. -> (list, [(name, attached|unchanged|replaced)])."""
    out, said = [dict(x) for x in have], []
    for x in new:
        e = {k: v for k, v in x.items() if k != "tmp"}
        i = next((k for k, y in enumerate(out) if y["name"] == x["name"]), None)
        if i is None:
            out.append(e)
            said.append((x["name"], "attached"))
        elif out[i]["sha256"] == x["sha256"]:
            said.append((x["name"], "unchanged"))
        elif replace:
            out[i] = e
            said.append((x["name"], "replaced"))
        else:
            raise Refused(f"{full} already has a supporting file {x['name']} with other bytes; "
                          f"`cc-docs attach {full} <file> --replace` swaps it")
    return out, said


def check_attachments(reg, num, rev, lst):
    """Refuse a revision's list that would pass a hosting cap, with the cap it passes."""
    if len(lst) > ATTACH_REV_CAP:
        raise Refused(f"{num}-{rev} would carry {len(lst)} supporting files, over {ATTACH_REV_CAP} a revision; zip some")
    blobs = {x["sha256"]: x["bytes"] for x in lst}
    for n, d in reg["documents"].items():
        for r in d["revisions"]:
            if (n, r["rev"]) != (num, rev):
                blobs.update((x["sha256"], x["bytes"]) for x in r.get("attachments") or ())
    total = sum(blobs.values())
    if total > ATTACH_TOTAL_CAP:
        raise Refused(f"the library's supporting files would come to {total >> 20} MiB, over the "
                      f"{ATTACH_TOTAL_CAP >> 20} MiB the mirror's GitHub repo is kept under; nothing attached")


def carry_attachments(prev, describes, new, full):
    """What a new revision starts from: the one before's supporting files, the names this filing attaches taken
    out, and none when the two describe different board revisions. Says on stderr what it carried or dropped."""
    have = (prev or {}).get("attachments") or []
    if not have:
        return []
    if describes and prev.get("describes") and describes != prev["describes"]:
        print(f"cc-docs: {full} describes {describes}, and {prev['rev']} described {prev['describes']}, so "
              f"{prev['rev']}'s {len(have)} supporting file(s) stay on {prev['rev']} and are not carried",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return []
    names = {x["name"] for x in new}
    kept = [dict(x, carried_from=x.get("carried_from") or prev["rev"]) for x in have if x["name"] not in names]
    if kept:
        print(f"cc-docs: {full} carries {len(kept)} supporting file(s) from {prev['rev']}: "
              f"{', '.join(x['name'] for x in kept)}", file=sys.stderr)
    return kept


def rev_of(reg, number):
    """(document, revision) for PPP-NNNN-R, or for PPP-NNNN its current revision."""
    m = NUM.match(number or "")
    if m and not m.group(3):
        d = get_doc(reg, number)
        return d, current(d)
    return get_rev(reg, number)


def cmd_attach(a):
    if not a.files and not a.remove:
        raise Refused("name a file to attach, or --remove <name>")
    staged = stage_attachments(a.files)
    try:
        with Lock():
            reg = load()
            d, r = rev_of(reg, a.number)
            full = f"{d['number']}-{r['rev']}"
            lst, said = list(r.get("attachments") or []), []
            for name in a.remove or ():
                if not any(x["name"] == name for x in lst):
                    raise Refused(f"{full} has no supporting file {name!r}")
                lst = [x for x in lst if x["name"] != name]
                said.append((name, "removed"))
            lst, got = merge_attachments(lst, staged, a.replace, full)
            said += got
            check_attachments(reg, d["number"], r["rev"], lst)
            staged.commit()
            if lst:
                r["attachments"] = lst
            else:
                r.pop("attachments", None)
            save(reg)
            write_views(reg, set(d["visibility"]) - {"owner"})
    finally:
        staged.close()
    for name, what in said:
        print(f"{full}\t{name}\t{what}")
    return 0


# ── a text revision's PDF ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def cmd_pdf(a):
    """The PDF of a revision filed without one (a Markdown revision whose PDF a renderer makes after filing), filed the
    way `file` files one: stamped unless its text carries its own number or the document is --no-stamp, read-only,
    recorded on that revision with its print, pages and bytes. A revision that has its PDF is refused: a filed copy
    is never rewritten. Another number quoted in its text is not refused: it is the owner's Markdown, which may name
    other documents."""
    src = os.path.abspath(a.pdf)
    if not os.path.isfile(src):
        raise Refused(f"{a.pdf}: no such file")
    text = pdftext(src)
    fp = fingerprint(src, text)
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        d, r = get_rev(reg, a.number)
        full = f"{d['number']}-{r['rev']}"
        if r.get("file"):
            raise Refused(f"{full} has its PDF already; a filed revision is never rewritten")
        rel = os.path.join("files", d["project"], f"{full}_{slugify(d['title'])}.pdf")
        dst = os.path.join(ROOT, rel)
        if os.path.exists(dst):
            raise Refused(f"{dst} exists; a filed revision is never rewritten")
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
        tmp = dst + ".part"
        carried = set(m.group(0).split()[0] for m in STAMP.finditer(text))
        if d.get("stamp") is False:
            how = "none"
            shutil.copy(src, tmp)
        elif full in carried:
            how = "carried"
            shutil.copy(src, tmp)
        else:
            how = "overlay"
            try:
                date = datetime.date.fromisoformat(r.get("date") or "")
            except ValueError:
                date = datetime.date.today()
            stamp(src, tmp, " · ".join([full] + ([r["describes"]] if r.get("describes") else []) + [stampdate(date)]))
        os.chmod(tmp, 0o444)
        os.replace(tmp, dst)
        with open(dst, "rb") as f:
            sha = hashlib.sha256(f.read()).hexdigest()
        r.update(file=rel, fingerprint=fp, sha256=sha, stamped=how, pages=pages(dst), bytes=os.path.getsize(dst),
                 pdf_at=utcnow())
        save(reg)
        write_views(reg, set(d.get("visibility", ())) - {"owner"})
    print(f"{full}\t{dst}\tfiled", flush=True)
    return 0


def spawn_check():
    """With DOCS_CHECK_CHANNEL set, `cc-docs check --post` detached, so the maker that filed is not held up."""
    if not conf("DOCS_CHECK_CHANNEL"):
        return
    try:
        subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, os.path.realpath(__file__), "check", "--post"], stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                         stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, start_new_session=True,
                         env=dict(os.environ, CC_DOCS_ROOT=ROOT))
    except OSError:
        pass


def cmd_number(a):
    describes = check_describes(a.describes)
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        proj, num, d, rev = plan(reg, a)   # a project it would create is not saved: `number` reserves nothing
    full = f"{num}-{rev}"
    if a.tex:
        st = " · ".join([full] + ([describes] if describes else []) + [stampdate(datetime.date.today())])
        print(f"\\def\\docnumber{{{full}}}\\def\\docstamp{{{st}}}")
    else:
        print(full)
    return 0


def rename_project(reg, name, new):
    """Give a project a new name or group; its number, documents and files stay as they are."""
    p = find_project(reg, name)
    if not p:
        raise Refused(f"no project {name!r}")
    group, sub = split_name(new)
    q = find_project(reg, new) if group is not None else next(
        (x for x, d in reg["projects"].items() if not d.get("group") and d["name"].lower() == sub.lower()), None)
    if q and q != p:
        raise Refused(f"project {new!r} already has number {q}")
    if not sub or group == "":
        raise Refused(f"project name {new!r} needs a name on each side of the /")
    if group is None and group_projects(reg, sub):
        raise Refused(f"{sub!r} is a group already; name the project inside it, {sub}/<name>")
    flat = find_project(reg, group) if group else None
    if flat and flat != p and not reg["projects"][flat].get("group"):
        raise Refused(f"project {flat} is named {group!r}: put it in the group first")
    reg["projects"][p].update(name=sub, group=group)
    return p


def cmd_project(a):
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        if a.rename:
            p = rename_project(reg, a.name, a.rename)
        elif not a.number and not find_project(reg, a.name) and group_projects(reg, a.name):
            # brief: "a group lists its sub-projects"
            for q in group_projects(reg, a.name):
                d = reg["projects"][q]
                print(f"{q}\t{full_name(d)}\t{d['kind']}" + (f"\t{d['member']}" if d.get("member") else ""))
            return 0
        else:
            p = make_project(reg, a.name, a.number, a.kind, a.member)
        save(reg)
        if a.rename:
            write_views(reg, {reg["projects"][p]["workspace"]} - {None})
    d = reg["projects"][p]
    print(f"{p}\t{full_name(d)}\t{d['kind']}" + (f"\t{d['member']}" if d.get("member") else ""))
    return 0


def search(reg, query):
    """-> [(docnum, rev-or-None)] best matches for a number or words."""
    q = " ".join(query).strip()
    m = NUM.match(q)
    if m:
        num = f"{m.group(1)}-{m.group(2)}"
        return [(num, m.group(3))] if num in reg["documents"] else []
    words = [w for w in re.findall(r"[a-z0-9]+", q.lower()) if w not in STOP]
    if not words:
        return []
    scored = []
    for num, d in reg["documents"].items():
        if d["title"].lower() == q.lower():
            scored.append((100, num))
            continue
        hay = set(re.findall(r"[a-z0-9]+", " ".join([d["title"], full_name(reg["projects"].get(d["project"], {"name": ""})),
                                                     d.get("source") or ""]).lower()))
        tw = set(re.findall(r"[a-z0-9]+", d["title"].lower()))
        hit = sum(1 for w in words if w in hay)
        if hit == len(words):
            scored.append((hit + sum(1 for w in words if w in tw) / 10, num))
    if not scored:
        return []
    top = max(s for s, _ in scored)
    return [(n, None) for s, n in sorted(scored) if s == top]


def cmd_find(a):
    reg = load()
    hits = search(reg, a.query)
    if not hits:
        print(f"cc-docs: no document matches {' '.join(a.query)!r}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if len(hits) > 1:
        for n, _ in hits:
            print(f"{n}-{current(reg['documents'][n])['rev']}\t{reg['documents'][n]['title']}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    n, rev = hits[0]
    d = reg["documents"][n]
    r = next((x for x in d["revisions"] if x["rev"] == rev), None) if rev else current(d)
    if not r:
        print(f"cc-docs: {n} has no revision {rev}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    print(os.path.join(ROOT, r["file"]))
    return 0


def cmd_list(a):
    reg = load()
    proj = find_project(reg, a.project) if a.project else None
    projs = {proj} if proj else set(group_projects(reg, a.project)) if a.project else None   # a group lists them all
    if a.project and not projs:
        print(f"cc-docs: no project {a.project!r}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    for n in sorted(reg["documents"]):
        d = reg["documents"][n]
        if projs and d["project"] not in projs:
            continue
        r = current(d)
        print(f"{n}-{r['rev']}\t{r['date']}\towner{'+' + d['member'] if d.get('member') else ''}\t{d['title']}")
    return 0


def check_describes(b):
    if b and not BOARD.match(b):
        raise Refused(f"--describes {b!r} is not a board revision like PCB-0001-B")
    return b or None


def parse_cost(items):
    """--cost step=usd, once per step -> {"total", "steps": [{"step", "usd"}]} in the order given, or None."""
    steps = []
    for it in items or ():
        step, _, usd = it.partition("=")
        step = step.strip().lower()
        try:
            v = float(usd)
        except ValueError:
            v = -1.0
        if not STEP.match(step) or not 0 <= v < 1e6 or any(x["step"] == step for x in steps):
            raise Refused(f"--cost {it!r} is not one step=usd (e.g. draft=0.80), each step once")
        steps.append({"step": step, "usd": round(v, 4)})
    return {"total": round(sum(x["usd"] for x in steps), 4), "steps": steps} if steps else None


def viewer_ok(v):
    if v != "owner" and not WID.match(v or ""):
        raise Refused(f"no viewer {v!r}: the owner, or a member's workspace id")
    return v


def visible(d, viewer):
    return viewer == "owner" or viewer in d.get("visibility", ())


def starred_by(d):
    """Viewer ids that starred d. A document filed before stars were per viewer holds `starred`, the owner's."""
    return list(d.get("starred_by") or (["owner"] if d.get("starred") else []))


def get_rev(reg, full):
    m = NUM.match(full or "")
    d = reg["documents"].get(f"{m.group(1)}-{m.group(2)}") if m and m.group(3) else None
    r = next((x for x in d["revisions"] if x["rev"] == m.group(3)), None) if d else None
    if not r:
        raise Refused(f"no revision {full!r}: give PPP-NNNN-R")
    return d, r


def cmd_star(a):
    viewer = viewer_ok(a.viewer)
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        d = reg["documents"].get(a.number)
        if not d or not visible(d, viewer):   # a document the viewer cannot see answers as one that does not exist
            raise Refused(f"no document {a.number!r}")
        who = [v for v in starred_by(d) if v != viewer] + ([viewer] if a.state == "on" else [])
        d["starred_by"] = sorted(who)
        d.pop("starred", None)
        save(reg)
        write_views(reg, set(d["visibility"]) - {"owner"})
    print(f"{a.number}\t{'starred' if a.state == 'on' else 'not starred'}")
    return 0


def public_hook(state, token, full):
    """Tell DOCS_PUBLIC_HOOK, where public links are served, that a token is on or off: `<cmd> on|off <token>
    <PPP-NNNN-R>`, 30 s. (True, its last stdout line) when it exits 0, else (False, why); unset, (True, "")."""
    cmd = conf("DOCS_PUBLIC_HOOK")
    if not cmd:
        return True, ""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(shlex.split(cmd) + [state, token, full], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
    except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        return False, str(e)
    lines = (r.stdout if r.returncode == 0 else (r.stderr.strip() or r.stdout)).strip().splitlines()
    return r.returncode == 0, (lines[-1] if lines else f"exit {r.returncode}")


def revoke_dropped(dropped):
    """Stop, where they are served, the public links a move or retire took out of the register (their old number is
    never handed out again, so a link left on answers 404 once the site's register moves on)."""
    for full, token in dropped:
        ok, why = public_hook("off", token, full)
        if not ok:
            print(f"{full}\tits public link still answers where it is served ({why}): "
                  f"run `{conf('DOCS_PUBLIC_HOOK')} off {token} {full}`", file=sys.stderr)


def cmd_public(a):
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        d, r = get_rev(reg, a.number)
        full = f"{d['number']}-{r['rev']}"
        if a.state == "on":
            # brief: "going public mints an unguessable token for exactly one revision"
            r.setdefault("public_token", secrets.token_urlsafe(24))
        elif r.get("public_token"):
            # brief: "a revoked link stops working at once": the served link goes first, and if it can't, nothing changes
            ok, why = public_hook("off", r["public_token"], full)
            if not ok:
                raise Refused(f"{full} is still public: DOCS_PUBLIC_HOOK could not stop its link ({why})")
            # brief: "going private deletes it for good"
            r.pop("public_token")
        d.pop("public", None)
        save(reg)
        write_views(reg, set(d["visibility"]) - {"owner"})
    token = r.get("public_token")
    if not token:
        print("private")
        return 0
    print(token)
    ok, url = public_hook("on", token, full)
    if not ok:
        print(f"{full}: DOCS_PUBLIC_HOOK could not serve its link yet ({url}); `public {full} on` again retries",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if url:
        print(url)
    return 0


def public_file(reg, token, full):
    """The filed copy a public link serves, or None: the token must be that one revision's, and still held."""
    try:
        d, r = get_rev(reg, full)
    except Refused:
        return None
    held = r.get("public_token") or ""
    return os.path.join(ROOT, r["file"]) if held and secrets.compare_digest(held, token) else None


def cmd_token(a):
    f = public_file(load(), a.token, a.number)
    if f:
        print(f)
    return 0 if f else 1


_PAGE_COUNTS = {}


def _pages(f):
    """pages(), remembered: a filed copy is never rewritten, and a revision filed before `pages` was recorded
    would otherwise cost a pdfinfo on every library() a long-running caller makes."""
    if f not in _PAGE_COUNTS:
        _PAGE_COUNTS[f] = pages(f)
    return _PAGE_COUNTS[f]


def library(reg, viewer):
    """What `viewer` may see, and nothing else: a member never gets another workspace's document, project, star
    or any public token."""
    owner = viewer == "owner"
    host = os.uname().nodename
    home = os.path.expanduser("~")
    docs = []
    for n in sorted(reg["documents"]):
        d = reg["documents"][n]
        if not visible(d, viewer) or not d["revisions"]:
            continue
        revs = []
        for r in d["revisions"]:
            f = os.path.join(ROOT, r["file"]) if r.get("file") else None    # None: a text revision not rendered yet
            out = {"rev": r["rev"], "date": r["date"], "note": r.get("note"), "file": f and f"/files/{n}-{r['rev']}.pdf",
                   "pages": r.get("pages") or (f and _pages(f)), "bytes": r.get("bytes") or (os.path.getsize(f) if f and os.path.exists(f) else 0),
                   "describes": r.get("describes"), "cost": r.get("cost"),
                   "public": owner and bool(r.get("public_token"))}
            if owner and r.get("public_token"):
                out["token"] = r["public_token"]
            # a workspace's filing is its own words, not the box's: the owner is told whose they are
            if owner and isinstance(r.get("filer"), dict) and r["filer"].get("member"):
                out["filed_by"] = r["filer"]["member"]
            revs.append(out)
        src = d.get("source")
        if src and src.startswith(home + "/"):
            src = "~" + src[len(home):]
        docs.append({"number": n, "project": d["project"], "title": d["title"], "current": d["revisions"][-1]["rev"],
                     "starred": viewer in starred_by(d), "access": list(d.get("visibility", ["owner"])),
                     "source": f"{host}:{src}" if src else None, "revisions": revs})
    projs = sorted({d["project"] for d in docs} | (set(reg["projects"]) if owner else set()))
    return {"viewer": {"id": viewer, "role": "owner" if owner else "member"},
            "projects": [dict({"number": p, "name": reg["projects"][p]["name"]},
                              **({"group": reg["projects"][p]["group"]} if reg["projects"][p].get("group") else {}))
                         for p in projs],
            "documents": docs}


def cmd_library(a):
    json.dump(library(load(), viewer_ok(a.viewer)), sys.stdout, indent=1)
    print()
    return 0


def retire_record(reg, key, entry, why):
    """Keep what a fold or a retire takes out as retired/<key>.json, and mark a document number as never reused."""
    os.makedirs(os.path.join(ROOT, "retired"), mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    at = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=os.path.join(ROOT, "retired"), prefix=".retired.")
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
        json.dump(dict(why, at=at, entry=entry), f, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
        f.write("\n")
    os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(ROOT, "retired", key + ".json"))
    if NUM.match(key) and not NUM.match(key).group(3):
        reg.setdefault("retired", {})[key] = dict(why, at=at)


def prune_views(wids, rels):
    """Take the filed copies at rels out of each view, before write_views links what the register now holds."""
    for wid in wids:
        for rel in rels:
            f = os.path.join(ROOT, "ws", wid, rel)
            if os.path.lexists(f):
                os.unlink(f)


def get_doc(reg, num):
    m = NUM.match(num or "")
    d = reg["documents"].get(num) if m and not m.group(3) else None
    if not d:
        raise Refused(f"no document {num!r}: give PPP-NNNN")
    return d


def cmd_fold(a):
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        keep = get_doc(reg, a.keep)
        others = [get_doc(reg, n) for n in a.other]
        docs = [keep] + others
        if len({d["number"] for d in docs}) != len(docs):
            raise Refused("a document is named twice")
        if any(d["project"] != keep["project"] for d in others):
            raise Refused(f"every document must be under {keep['number']}'s project {keep['project']}")
        if any(d.get("retired_revs") for d in docs):
            raise Refused("a document with a retired revision cannot be folded: its letter would be handed out again")
        # brief: "ordered oldest first by revision date (ties go by the order given) ... its current revision must
        # stay the newest, so the next build of its source still matches it"
        last = current(keep)
        rest = sorted(((r["date"], i, j, d, r) for i, d in enumerate(docs) for j, r in enumerate(d["revisions"])
                       if r is not last), key=lambda x: x[:3])
        late = [f"{d['number']}-{r['rev']}" for dt, _, _, d, r in rest if dt > last["date"]]
        if late:
            raise Refused(f"{', '.join(late)} is dated after {keep['number']}-{last['rev']}, which must stay the newest")
        order = [(d, r) for *_, d, r in rest] + [(keep, last)]
        slug = slugify(keep["title"])
        moves, revs, dropped = [], [], []
        for i, (d, r) in enumerate(order):
            new = dict(r, rev=letter(i), file=os.path.join("files", keep["project"], f"{keep['number']}-{letter(i)}_{slug}.pdf"))
            if (d is not keep or r["rev"] != new["rev"]) and new.get("public_token"):
                dropped.append((f"{d['number']}-{r['rev']}", new.pop("public_token")))
            if d is not keep:
                new["folded_from"] = f"{d['number']}-{r['rev']}"
            moves.append((f"{d['number']}-{r['rev']}", r["file"], new["file"]))
            revs.append(new)
        old = {o for _, o, _ in moves}
        missing = [o for o in old if not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(ROOT, o))]
        clash = [n for *_, n in moves if n not in old and os.path.lexists(os.path.join(ROOT, n))]
        if missing or clash:
            raise Refused(f"{(missing + clash)[0]} is {'missing' if missing else 'in the way'}; nothing changed")
        # the site pins a link to (number, letter), and fold hands a dropped token's letter to another revision, so the
        # served link must be off before the letters move: else it would serve a revision nobody made public
        for full, token in dropped:
            ok, why = public_hook("off", token, full)
            if not ok:
                raise Refused(f"{full}'s public link could not be stopped where it is served ({why}); nothing was folded")
            print(f"{full}\tits public link stops working", file=sys.stderr)
        for d in others:
            retire_record(reg, d["number"], d, {"folded_into": keep["number"]})
        # every copy steps aside to a temporary name first, since a new name may be an old one still in place
        for k, (_, o, n) in enumerate(moves):
            os.rename(os.path.join(ROOT, o), os.path.join(ROOT, n + f".fold{k}"))
        for k, (_, o, n) in enumerate(moves):
            os.rename(os.path.join(ROOT, n + f".fold{k}"), os.path.join(ROOT, n))
        keep["revisions"] = revs
        wids = set().union(*(set(d.get("visibility", ())) for d in docs)) - {"owner"}
        for d in others:
            del reg["documents"][d["number"]]
        save(reg)
        prune_views(wids, old)
        write_views(reg, wids)
    for (was, _, n), r in zip(moves, revs):
        print(f"{was}\t{keep['number']}-{r['rev']}\t{os.path.join(ROOT, n)}")
    return 0


def read_from(path):
    """--from TSV: {PPP-NNNN: (/abs/path.tex, nearest)}; '#' comments, blank lines and 'none' skipped. A third column
    `nearest` says the .tex is the nearest source found, not an exact match of the filed PDF."""
    out = {}
    with open(path) as f:
        for ln in f:
            ln = ln.strip()
            if not ln or ln.startswith("#"):
                continue
            num, tex, kind = (ln.split("\t") + ["", ""])[:3]
            num, tex, kind = num.strip(), tex.strip(), kind.strip().lower()
            if NUM.match(num) and not NUM.match(num).group(3) and tex and tex.lower() != "none":
                out[num] = (os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(tex)), kind == "nearest")
    return out


def has_manifest(tar):
    import tarfile
    try:
        with tarfile.open(tar) as t:
            return MANIFEST in t.getnames()
    except (OSError, tarfile.TarError):
        return False


def source_drift(old, new):
    """The files of the kept tarball `old` (its .source.json aside) whose bytes are nowhere in the tarball `new`: what
    a re-keep would lose. A file that only moved (an old _ext/ path now under _style/) is not drift. -> [name]."""
    import hashlib
    import tarfile

    def contents(tar):
        out = {}
        with tarfile.open(tar) as t:
            for m in t.getmembers():
                if m.isfile() and m.name != MANIFEST:
                    out[m.name] = hashlib.sha256(t.extractfile(m).read()).hexdigest()
        return out
    try:
        have = set(contents(new).values())
        return sorted(n for n, h in contents(old).items() if h not in have)
    except (OSError, tarfile.TarError) as e:
        return [f"(unreadable: {e})"]


def cmd_backfill(a):
    import argparse
    picks = read_from(a.from_) if getattr(a, "from_", None) else {}
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        changed = False
        nearest = set()
        for num, (tex, near) in picks.items():
            d = reg["documents"].get(num)
            if d and (not d.get("source") or not os.path.exists(d["source"])):
                d["source"], changed = tex, True
            if d and near and d.get("source") == tex:
                nearest.add(num)
        if changed:
            save(reg)
        todo = [(num, dict(reg["documents"][num]), dict(current(reg["documents"][num])))
                for num in sorted(reg["documents"]) if current(reg["documents"][num])]
    cmd, cache, passes = conf("DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK"), read_checks().get("passes", {}), {}
    for num, d, r in todo:
        full = f"{num}-{r['rev']}"
        tar = os.path.join(ROOT, r["sources"]) if r.get("sources") else None
        if tar and os.path.isfile(tar) and not any(n.endswith(".tex") for n in r.get("source_files") or ()):
            continue                 # a kept source that is not LaTeX: nothing to compile, nothing to add
        if tar and os.path.isfile(tar) and has_manifest(tar):
            if not cmd:
                continue
            sha = sha_of(tar)
            if sha in cache:
                continue
            v, ran = run_check(cmd, tar)
            if v["ok"]:
                passes[sha] = {"at": utcnow(), "engine": v.get("engine")}
                continue
        member = d.get("member")
        ns = argparse.Namespace(source=d.get("source"), latex=None, origin=member or None,
                                trees=member_trees(member, "") if member else None)
        files = find_sources(ns, r.get("from") or "")
        if not files:
            print(f"{full}\tno source\t{d.get('source') or 'no --source recorded'}")
            continue
        st, why = stage_sources(files, full, ns.trees)
        if not st:
            print(f"{full}\tnot kept\t{why}")
            continue
        try:
            # a tarball kept at filing is that PDF's exact source: a re-keep may add to it (a manifest, a style
            # tree, fonts) but never swap a file for what the working tree holds now
            drift = source_drift(tar, st.tar) if tar and os.path.isfile(tar) else []
            if drift:
                print(f"{full}\tnot kept\tsource changed since filing: {', '.join(drift[:5])}")
                continue
            with Lock():
                reg = load()
                cur = current(reg["documents"].get(num) or {"revisions": []})
                if not cur or cur["rev"] != r["rev"]:
                    print(f"{full}\tnot kept\tits document changed while it was checked")
                    continue
                cur.update(st.commit(d["project"], full), sources_backfilled=True)
                if num in nearest:
                    cur["source_nearest"] = True     # never shown as the exact source of the filed PDF
                elif num in picks and d.get("source") == picks[num][0]:
                    cur.pop("source_nearest", None)  # an exact pick
                save(reg)
                n = len(cur["source_files"])
            print(f"{full}\tkept\t{n} file(s)" + (f", {cur['source_engine']}" if cur.get("source_engine") else "")
                  + (", compiles" if cur.get("source_checked") else ""))
        finally:
            st.close()
    record_passes(passes)
    return 0


def summary(problems, missing, n_ok, n_all):
    """The --post text: counts, the failing numbers, the missing packages, under 800 characters."""
    kinds = {}
    for full, kind, _ in problems:
        kinds.setdefault(kind, []).append(full)
    head = f"Library sources: {n_ok} of {n_all} kept sources compile."
    parts = []
    for kind in sorted(kinds):
        nums = kinds[kind]
        shown = ", ".join(nums[:12]) + (f" and {len(nums) - 12} more" if len(nums) > 12 else "")
        parts.append(f"{kind.capitalize()} ({len(nums)}): {shown}.")
    if missing:
        parts.append("Missing TeX packages: " + ", ".join(sorted(missing)[:20]) + ".")
    text = " ".join([head] + parts)
    return text if len(text) < 790 else text[:780].rsplit(" ", 1)[0] + " …"


def cmd_check(a):
    cmd = conf("DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK")
    if not cmd:
        raise Refused("DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK is not set, so there is nothing to compile a source with "
                      "(cc-config set DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK <command>)")
    os.makedirs(ROOT, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(ROOT, ".check.lock"), "w") as lf:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(lf, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except OSError:
            print("cc-docs: another check is running; this one stops")
            return 0
        reg, checks = load(), read_checks()
        cache, passes = checks.get("passes", {}), {}
        problems, missing, n_ok, n_all = [], set(), 0, 0
        for num in sorted(reg["documents"]):
            d = reg["documents"][num]
            r = current(d)
            if not r:
                continue
            full = f"{num}-{r['rev']}"
            tar = os.path.join(ROOT, r["sources"]) if r.get("sources") else None
            if not tar or not os.path.isfile(tar):
                problems.append((full, "no source", d.get("source") or "no --source recorded"))
                continue
            if not any(n.endswith(".tex") for n in r.get("source_files") or ()):
                problems.append((full, "no .tex", ", ".join((r.get("source_files") or [])[:3]) or "empty"))
                continue
            n_all += 1
            sha = sha_of(tar)
            if sha in cache:
                n_ok += 1
                continue
            v, ran = run_check(cmd, tar)
            if v["ok"]:
                n_ok += 1
                passes[sha] = {"at": utcnow(), "engine": v.get("engine")}
                continue
            problems.append((full, "fails" if ran else "cannot check", first_error(v, ran)))
            missing |= {str(x) for x in v.get("missing") or [] if x}
        record_passes(passes)
        for p in problems:
            print("\t".join(p))
        if missing:
            print("missing TeX packages: " + ", ".join(sorted(missing)))
        print(f"{n_ok} of {n_all} kept sources compile")
        if a.post and problems:
            post_check(problems, missing, n_ok, n_all, checks.get("post") or {})
    return 1 if problems else 0


def post_check(problems, missing, n_ok, n_all, last):
    """Post the summary when the problem set changed since the last post, or that post is over 20 h old."""
    chan = conf("DOCS_CHECK_CHANNEL")
    if not chan:
        return
    digest = hashlib.sha256(("\n".join(f"{f}\t{k}" for f, k, _ in problems) + "\n" + ",".join(sorted(missing)))
                            .encode()).hexdigest()[:12]
    now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)
    try:
        age = now - datetime.datetime.strptime(last.get("at", ""), "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ").replace(
            tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)
    except ValueError:
        age = None
    if digest == last.get("digest") and age is not None and age < datetime.timedelta(hours=20):
        return
    # cc-slack posts one --id once, ever: the minute goes in it, so the 20-hour reminder of the same set is not a replay
    pid = f"docs-check-{digest}-{now.strftime('%Y%m%d%H%M')}"
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([os.environ.get("CC_SLACK_BIN") or "cc-slack", "post", "-c", chan, "--id", pid, "--major",
                            summary(problems, missing, n_ok, n_all)], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120,
                           stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        print(f"cc-docs: the check's summary was not posted: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return
    if r.returncode != 0:
        print(f"cc-docs: the check's summary was not posted: {(r.stderr.strip() or f'exit {r.returncode}')[:300]}",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return
    update_checks(lambda c: c.update(post={"digest": digest, "at": now.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")}))


def cmd_retire(a):
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        m = NUM.match(a.number or "")
        if m and m.group(3):
            d, r = get_rev(reg, a.number)
            gone = d["revisions"] if len(d["revisions"]) == 1 else [r]
        else:
            d = get_doc(reg, a.number)
            gone = d["revisions"]
        whole = gone is d["revisions"]
        key = d["number"] if whole else a.number
        retire_record(reg, key, d if whole else r, {"retired": key})
        for x in gone:
            dst = os.path.join(ROOT, "retired", x["file"])
            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
            os.rename(os.path.join(ROOT, x["file"]), dst)
        if whole:
            del reg["documents"][d["number"]]
        else:
            d["revisions"].remove(r)
            d.setdefault("retired_revs", []).append(r["rev"])
        save(reg)
        wids = set(d.get("visibility", ())) - {"owner"}
        prune_views(wids, [x["file"] for x in gone])
        write_views(reg, wids)
    revoke_dropped([(f"{d['number']}-{x['rev']}", x["public_token"]) for x in gone if x.get("public_token")])
    for x in gone:
        print(f"{d['number']}-{x['rev']}\tretired\t{os.path.join(ROOT, 'retired', x['file'])}")
    return 0


def cmd_move(a):
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        d = get_doc(reg, a.number)
        old = d["number"]
        # brief: "makes or reuses the sub-project under the group", as `file --project` does
        proj = find_project(reg, a.project)
        if not proj:
            if re.fullmatch(r"\d{3}", a.project):
                raise Refused(f"no project {a.project}")
            proj = make_project(reg, a.project, None, a.kind, None)
        if proj == d["project"]:
            raise Refused(f"{old} is already under project {proj}")
        if reg["projects"][proj].get("workspace") != reg["projects"][d["project"]].get("workspace"):
            raise Refused(f"project {proj} is seen by other people than project {d['project']}; a move never changes that")
        new = next_doc(reg, proj)
        slug = slugify(d["title"])
        moves = [(r, os.path.join("files", proj, f"{new}-{r['rev']}_{slug}.pdf")) for r in d["revisions"]]
        missing = [r["file"] for r, _ in moves if not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(ROOT, r["file"]))]
        # a kept source moves with its revision, so its name keeps matching the PDF's
        srcs = [(r, os.path.join("sources", proj, f"{new}-{r['rev']}.tar.gz")) for r in d["revisions"]
                if r.get("sources") and os.path.isfile(os.path.join(ROOT, r["sources"]))]
        clash = [n for _, n in moves + srcs if os.path.lexists(os.path.join(ROOT, n))]
        if missing or clash:
            raise Refused(f"{(missing + clash)[0]} is {'missing' if missing else 'in the way'}; nothing changed")
        # brief: "the old number is retired and never reused, and a note of the old number is kept on the document"
        retire_record(reg, old, d, {"moved_to": new})
        os.makedirs(os.path.join(ROOT, "files", proj), exist_ok=True)
        for r, n in moves:
            os.rename(os.path.join(ROOT, r["file"]), os.path.join(ROOT, n))
        if srcs:
            os.makedirs(os.path.join(ROOT, "sources", proj), exist_ok=True)
        for r, n in srcs:
            os.rename(os.path.join(ROOT, r["sources"]), os.path.join(ROOT, n))
            r["sources"] = n
        gone, dropped = [r["file"] for r, _ in moves], []
        for r, n in moves:
            if r.get("public_token"):
                dropped.append((f"{old}-{r['rev']}", r.pop("public_token")))
                print(f"{old}-{r['rev']}\tits public link stops working", file=sys.stderr)
            r["file"] = n
        del reg["documents"][old]
        d.update(number=new, project=proj, moved_from=d.get("moved_from", []) + [old])
        reg["documents"][new] = d
        save(reg)
        wids = set(d.get("visibility", ())) - {"owner"}
        prune_views(wids, gone)
        write_views(reg, wids)
    revoke_dropped(dropped)
    for r, n in moves:
        print(f"{old}-{r['rev']}\t{new}-{r['rev']}\t{os.path.join(ROOT, n)}")
    return 0


# ── selfcheck ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ── a member workspace files across its socket ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Inside a member's sandbox ~/.cc/documents is that member's read-only view, so `file` and `number` there cannot
# write. They cross the workspace's own socket instead (across), as `cc-mail send` does: the daemon's member verb
# `docs` runs `cc-docs member <handle>` on the host with the handle it read off the socket, and member_ask decides.
HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
SLACKSOCK = os.path.join(os.environ.get("CC_SLACK_DIR") or os.path.join(HOME, ".cc", "slack"), "sock")
IN_SANDBOX = os.environ.get("CC_MEMBER_SANDBOX") == "1"
MEMBER_CAP = 64 << 20     # the largest PDF a workspace may file, in bytes
NOTE_CAP = 2000           # the longest note a workspace may file with a revision, in characters
MEMBER_WAIT = 300         # seconds the workspace waits on the host: stamping and printing a long PDF takes a while
HANDLE = re.compile(r"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,39}$")
ASK = {"op", "pdf", "title", "project", "source", "kind", "member", "describes", "note", "date", "cost", "no_stamp", "tex"}


def across(a):
    """`file` or `number` inside a member workspace: the flags as an ask on the member socket, the host's line back."""
    import socket
    ask = {"op": a.cmd, "title": a.title}
    for k in ("project", "kind", "member", "describes", "note", "date", "cost"):
        if getattr(a, k, None):
            ask[k] = getattr(a, k)
    if a.source:
        ask["source"] = os.path.abspath(a.source)
    if a.cmd == "file":
        ask["pdf"] = os.path.abspath(a.pdf)
        ask["no_stamp"] = bool(a.no_stamp)
    else:
        ask["tex"] = bool(a.tex)
    c = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
    c.settimeout(MEMBER_WAIT)
    try:
        c.connect(SLACKSOCK)
        c.sendall((json.dumps({"docs": ask}) + "\n").encode())
        buf = b""
        while not buf.endswith(b"\n"):
            d = c.recv(65536)
            if not d:
                break
            buf += d
        answer = json.loads(buf or b"{}")
    except Exception as e:
        print(f"cc-docs: nothing filed — the workspace's socket did not answer ({str(e)[:200]}): the host files for "
              "this workspace, and nothing there is listening", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if isinstance(answer, dict) and answer.get("ok"):
        print(str(answer.get("text") or ""))
        return 0
    print(f"cc-docs: {(answer.get('error') if isinstance(answer, dict) else '') or 'the host refused'}", file=sys.stderr)
    return 2


def member_trees(handle, files):
    """The directories a workspace may file from, resolved: its ~/dev/<h>, its track worktrees and its Slack files."""
    return [os.path.realpath(p) for p in (os.path.join(HOME, "dev", handle),
                                          os.path.join(HOME, ".cc", "worktrees", handle), files) if p]


def readable(trees, styles=None):
    """Where a member's source may be read from: its trees and the box's own style roots; None (anywhere) for
    the owner's."""
    if trees is None:
        return None
    return list(trees) + [os.path.realpath(r) for r, _ in (style_trees() if styles is None else styles)]


def within(path, trees):
    return any(path == t or path.startswith(t.rstrip("/") + "/") for t in trees)


def member_pdf(path, trees):
    """The bytes of a workspace's PDF, read from ONE fd: O_NOFOLLOW refuses a link as the last part, the fd's own
    /proc path must be inside the workspace (which catches a linked directory), and the read stops past the cap —
    so the file cannot be swapped between the check and the read (outbound.attach_bytes, the same reasoning)."""
    nope = f"{path} is not a file inside this workspace"
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    except OSError:
        raise Refused(nope)
    try:
        st = os.fstat(fd)
        try:
            real = os.readlink(f"/proc/self/fd/{fd}")
        except OSError:
            raise Refused(nope)
        if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode) or real.endswith(" (deleted)") or not within(real, trees):
            raise Refused(nope)
        if st.st_size > MEMBER_CAP:
            raise Refused(f"{path} is {st.st_size >> 20} MiB; a workspace files a PDF of {MEMBER_CAP >> 20} MiB at most")
        data = b""
        while len(data) <= MEMBER_CAP:
            chunk = os.read(fd, 1 << 20)
            if not chunk:
                break
            data += chunk
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    if len(data) > MEMBER_CAP:
        raise Refused(f"{path} grew past {MEMBER_CAP >> 20} MiB while it was read")
    if not data.startswith(b"%PDF-"):
        raise Refused(f"{path} is not a PDF; a workspace files PDFs only")
    return data


def member_project(reg, handle, named):
    """-> (project, kind, member) for plan(). The workspace's own project is the one its ask names when that one is
    its own, else its first; a workspace with none gets one named after it. Another member's project is refused.
    An owner project named from a workspace is not the workspace's to file into, so its own takes its place: a
    maker that set DOC_PROJECT for the host still files, under the member."""
    p = find_project(reg, named) if named else None
    if p and reg["projects"][p].get("member") == handle:
        return p, None, None
    if p and reg["projects"][p].get("member"):
        raise Refused(f"project {named!r} is another member's; a workspace files only under its own")
    own = sorted(q for q, d in reg["projects"].items() if d.get("member") == handle)
    if own:
        return own[0], None, None
    if find_project(reg, handle):
        raise Refused(f"project {handle!r} is not this workspace's, and it has none of its own to file under")
    return handle, "member", handle


def member_ask(handle, ask, files=""):
    """One workspace's `file` or `number`, decided on the host. `handle` is the daemon's, read off the socket the ask
    came on, and never the ask's; the ask may name its PDF, title, source, note, date, cost, board revision and
    whether to stamp. -> the line `file` or `number` prints. Refused: another member's project or --member, a PDF
    or source outside the workspace's own trees, anything but a PDF, one over MEMBER_CAP, any op but these two."""
    import argparse
    import contextlib
    import io
    # brief: "The host files only into the project that belongs to the asking workspace, identified by the socket,
    # never by anything the workspace says." `handle` is the socket's; the ask's `member` can only agree with it.
    if not HANDLE.match(handle or ""):
        raise Refused(f"no workspace {handle!r}")
    if not isinstance(ask, dict):
        raise Refused("docs wants one object")
    odd = sorted(str(k)[:40] for k in set(ask) - ASK)
    if odd:
        raise Refused(f"unknown key {', '.join(odd)} — the keys are {', '.join(sorted(ASK))}")
    op = ask.get("op")
    if op not in ("file", "number"):
        raise Refused(f"a workspace can file and number its documents, not {str(op)[:40]!r}; only the owner makes "
                      "anything public, stars for someone else, or makes a project")
    title, cost = ask.get("title"), ask.get("cost") or []
    if not isinstance(title, str) or not title.strip():
        raise Refused("a document needs a title")
    if not isinstance(cost, list) or not all(isinstance(c, str) for c in cost):
        raise Refused("cost is a list of <step>=<usd>")
    for k in ("project", "kind", "member", "describes", "note", "date", "source", "pdf"):
        if ask.get(k) is not None and not isinstance(ask[k], str):
            raise Refused(f"{k} must be a string")
    if ask.get("member") and ask["member"] != handle:
        raise Refused(f"a workspace files only for itself, not for {ask['member'][:40]!r}")
    if len(ask.get("note") or "") > NOTE_CAP:
        raise Refused(f"a note is at most {NOTE_CAP} characters")
    inside = os.path.join(HOME, ".cc", "slack", "files") + "/"
    here = lambda q: os.path.join(files, q[len(inside):]) if files and q.startswith(inside) else q   # the boundary's ~/.cc/slack is the member dir
    trees = member_trees(handle, files)
    source = ask.get("source")
    if source and not within(os.path.normpath(here(source)), trees):
        raise Refused(f"{source} is not a path inside this workspace")
    tmp = None
    try:
        if op == "file":
            data = member_pdf(here(str(ask.get("pdf") or "")), trees)
            os.makedirs(ROOT, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
            tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=ROOT, prefix=".incoming.")
            pdf = os.path.join(tmp, "in.pdf")
            with open(pdf, "wb") as f:
                f.write(data)
        a = argparse.Namespace(cmd=op, title=title.strip(), source=source or None, describes=ask.get("describes"),
                               note=ask.get("note"), date=ask.get("date"), cost=cost, no_stamp=bool(ask.get("no_stamp")),
                               tex=bool(ask.get("tex")), origin=ask.get("pdf"), pdf=pdf if op == "file" else None,
                               trees=trees, filer={"member": handle},
                               srcpath=os.path.normpath(here(source)) if source else None)
        with Lock():
            a.project, a.kind, a.member = member_project(load(), handle, ask.get("project"))
        out = io.StringIO()
        with contextlib.redirect_stdout(out):
            (cmd_file if op == "file" else cmd_number)(a)
        return out.getvalue().strip()
    finally:
        if tmp:
            shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)


def cmd_member(a):
    """The daemon's half of the member verb `docs`: the ask as JSON on stdin, the answer as JSON on stdout."""
    try:
        ask = json.loads(sys.stdin.read() or "null")
        print(json.dumps({"ok": True, "text": member_ask(a.handle, ask, a.files or "")}))
        return 0
    except (Refused, ValueError) as e:
        print(json.dumps({"ok": False, "error": str(e)}))
        return 2


def selfcheck():
    """The cases, in a config of their own: no key of the box's ~/.cc/config (a live DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK or
    DOCS_CHECK_CHANNEL) reaches them, and each case sets the keys it tests in the environment, which wins."""
    keys = ("CC_CONFIG", "DOCS_SOURCE_CHECK", "DOCS_TEX_TREES", "DOCS_CHECK_CHANNEL", "DOCS_PUBLIC_HOOK", "CC_SLACK_BIN",
            "TEXINPUTS")
    saved = {k: os.environ.pop(k, None) for k in keys}
    os.environ["CC_CONFIG"] = "/nonexistent/cc-docs-selfcheck-config"
    try:
        return _selfcheck()
    finally:
        for k, v in saved.items():
            if v is None:
                os.environ.pop(k, None)
            else:
                os.environ[k] = v


def _selfcheck():
    global ROOT, MEMBERS, HOME, IN_SANDBOX, SLACKSOCK, MEMBER_CAP, ATTACH_FILE_CAP, ATTACH_TOTAL_CAP, ATTACH_REV_CAP
    n = [0, 0]

    def ok(name, cond):
        n[0 if cond else 1] += 1
        print(("  ok   " if cond else "  FAIL ") + name)

    def mkpdf(d, name, body):
        """A one-page PDF saying `body`, built by pdflatex in d."""
        with open(os.path.join(d, name + ".tex"), "w") as f:
            f.write("\\documentclass{article}\\pagestyle{empty}\\begin{document}" + body + "\\end{document}\n")
        subprocess.run(["pdflatex", "-interaction=batchmode", name + ".tex"], cwd=d, capture_output=True)
        return os.path.join(d, name + ".pdf")

    def run(*args):
        out, err = sys.stdout, sys.stderr
        import io
        sys.stdout, sys.stderr = io.StringIO(), io.StringIO()
        try:
            rc = main(list(args))
        finally:
            o, e = sys.stdout.getvalue(), sys.stderr.getvalue()
            sys.stdout, sys.stderr = out, err
        return rc, o + e

    print("cc-docs selfcheck")
    ok("letters: A, H→J (I skipped), N→P (O skipped), Z, then AA", [letter(i) for i in (0, 8, 13, 23, 24, 25)]
       == ["A", "J", "P", "Z", "AA", "AB"])
    ok("slug: lowercase with hyphens", slugify("The Autobox: Explanation (v2)") == "the-autobox-explanation-v2")
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="cc-docs-sc-") as t:
        src = os.path.join(t, "src")
        os.makedirs(src)
        MEMBERS = os.path.join(t, "members")
        wid = "0123456789abcdef"
        os.makedirs(os.path.join(MEMBERS, "kid1"))
        with open(os.path.join(MEMBERS, "kid1", "workspace-id"), "w") as f:
            f.write(wid + "\n")
        # numbering: each case files into a register of its own
        ROOT = os.path.join(t, "r1")
        a = mkpdf(src, "a", "Alpha one")
        b = mkpdf(src, "b", "Beta one\\newpage Beta two\\newpage Beta three")
        rc, o = run("file", a, "--project", "Box", "--title", "Alpha doc")
        ok("a new project with no kind is refused, nothing filed", rc == 2 and not os.path.exists(regpath()))
        run("file", a, "--project", "Box", "--kind", "work", "--title", "Alpha doc")
        rc, o = run("file", b, "--project", "Box", "--title", "Beta doc")
        run("file", b, "--project", "Course X", "--kind", "course", "--title", "Beta doc")
        run("file", a, "--project", "Kid", "--member", "kid1", "--title", "Alpha doc")
        reg = load()
        ok("the first work project is 001, its documents 001-0001 then 001-0002",
           sorted(n for n, d in reg["documents"].items() if d["project"] == "001") == ["001-0001", "001-0002"])
        ok("a course project starts at 101, a member project at 901",
           reg["projects"]["101"]["name"] == "Course X" and reg["projects"]["901"]["member"] == "kid1")
        ok("a member document is visible to that member and the owner, an owner document to the owner only",
           reg["documents"]["901-0001"]["visibility"] == ["owner", wid] and reg["documents"]["001-0001"]["visibility"] == ["owner"])
        v = os.path.join(ROOT, "ws", wid)
        with open(os.path.join(v, "register.json")) as fh:
            view = json.load(fh)
        vf = os.path.join(v, view["documents"]["901-0001"]["revisions"][0]["file"])
        ok("the member's view holds its own document and project and none of the owner's",
           list(view["documents"]) == ["901-0001"] and list(view["projects"]) == ["901"])
        ok("the view's file is the filed copy, linked and not copied",
           os.path.samefile(vf, os.path.join(ROOT, reg["documents"]["901-0001"]["revisions"][0]["file"])))
        owner_root, ROOT = ROOT, v
        rc, o = run("find", "alpha")
        rc2, o2 = run("find", "001-0001")
        ROOT = owner_root
        ok("find inside the view finds the member's document and not the owner's",
           rc == 0 and o.strip() == vf and rc2 == 1)
        ok("no view is made for the owner's documents alone", sorted(os.listdir(os.path.join(ROOT, "ws"))) == [wid])
        f = os.path.join(ROOT, reg["documents"]["001-0002"]["revisions"][0]["file"])
        ok("the filed copy is named PPP-NNNN-R_slug.pdf, read-only", os.path.basename(f) == "001-0002-A_beta-doc.pdf"
           and (os.geteuid() == 0 or not os.access(f, os.W_OK)))
        ok("an unstamped PDF gets the stamp overlaid on every page, and the original is left alone",
           "001-0002-A" not in pdftext(b) and pages(f) == 3 and pdftext(f).count("001-0002-A · ") == 3)
        # the stamp is appended, not re-rendered: links, outline and metadata survive, on both cross-reference kinds
        def marks(path):
            p = _PDF(open(path, "rb").read())
            links = sum(p.get(x).get("Subtype") == "Link" for _, pg, _ in p.pages() for x in p.get(pg.get("Annots")) or [])
            info = subprocess.run(["pdfinfo", path], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout
            return links, "Outlines" in p.get(p.trailer["Root"]), "".join(re.findall(r"^Title:\s*(.*)$", info, re.M))
        body = ("\\tableofcontents\\section{One}\\label{a}See \\ref{b}.\\newpage\\section{Two}\\label{b}See \\ref{a}"
                " and \\url{https://example.org}.")
        for name, pre in (("xs", ""), ("xt", "\\pdfobjcompresslevel=0 ")):
            with open(os.path.join(src, name + ".tex"), "w") as fh:
                fh.write(pre + "\\documentclass{article}\\usepackage[pdftitle={Hyper doc}]{hyperref}\\begin{document}"
                         + body + "\\end{document}\n")
            for _ in range(2):
                subprocess.run(["pdflatex", "-interaction=batchmode", name + ".tex"], cwd=src, capture_output=True)
            h, hs = os.path.join(src, name + ".pdf"), os.path.join(src, name + "-s.pdf")
            stamp(h, hs, "001-0009-A · 25 Sep 2026")
            with open(h, "rb") as f1, open(hs, "rb") as f2:
                kept = f2.read().startswith(f1.read())
            ok(f"a stamp keeps links, outline and title ({'classic table' if pre else 'xref stream'}), appended to "
               "the original bytes", marks(h)[0] > 0 and marks(hs) == marks(h) == (marks(h)[0], True, "Hyper doc")
               and kept and pdftext(hs).count("001-0009-A · 25 Sep 2026") == 2)
        real, err = overlay, sys.stderr
        import io
        sys.stderr = io.StringIO()

        def unreadable(*_):
            raise _Unreadable("encrypted")
        try:
            globals()["overlay"] = unreadable
            stamp(h, os.path.join(src, "fb.pdf"), "001-0009-B · 25 Sep 2026")
        finally:
            globals()["overlay"], said, sys.stderr = real, sys.stderr.getvalue(), err
        fb = os.path.join(src, "fb.pdf")
        ok("a PDF the appender cannot read is re-rendered instead, stamped, and says its links are lost",
           pdftext(fb).count("001-0009-B · 25 Sep 2026") == 2 and marks(fb)[0] == 0 and "links and outline are lost" in said)
        # stars, public links and what each viewer is sent: r1 as the cases above left it, rebuilt here on its own
        ROOT = os.path.join(t, "r1s")
        run("file", a, "--project", "Box", "--kind", "work", "--title", "Alpha doc")
        run("file", a, "--project", "Kid", "--member", "kid1", "--title", "Kid doc")
        run("star", "001-0001", "on")
        run("star", "901-0001", "on", "--viewer", wid)
        rc, o = run("star", "001-0001", "on", "--viewer", wid)
        reg = load()
        ok("stars are per viewer, and a member cannot star a document it cannot see",
           reg["documents"]["001-0001"]["starred_by"] == ["owner"] and reg["documents"]["901-0001"]["starred_by"] == [wid]
           and rc == 2)
        rc, o = run("library", "--viewer", wid)
        mine = json.loads(o)
        ok("a member's library holds its own documents and projects and nothing of the owner's",
           rc == 0 and [d["number"] for d in mine["documents"]] == ["901-0001"]
           and [p["number"] for p in mine["projects"]] == ["901"] and mine["viewer"]["role"] == "member"
           and mine["documents"][0]["starred"] is True)
        rc, o = run("library", "--viewer", "owner")
        own = json.loads(o)
        ok("the owner's library holds every document, with the owner's own stars only",
           [d["number"] for d in own["documents"]] == ["001-0001", "901-0001"]
           and [d["starred"] for d in own["documents"]] == [True, False] and own["viewer"]["role"] == "owner")
        rc, o = run("library", "--viewer", "fedcba9876543210")
        rc2, o2 = run("library", "--viewer", "someone")
        ok("an unknown workspace sees nothing, and a viewer that is not an id is refused",
           rc == 0 and json.loads(o)["documents"] == [] and json.loads(o)["projects"] == [] and rc2 == 2)
        rc, tok = run("public", "901-0001-A", "on")
        tok = tok.strip()
        rc2, again = run("public", "901-0001-A", "on")
        ok("public mints an unguessable token for the revision, and on again keeps it",
           rc == 0 and len(tok) >= 32 and again.strip() == tok)
        rc, o = run("token", tok, "901-0001-A")
        rc2, o2 = run("token", tok, "001-0001-A")
        rc3, o3 = run("token", tok[:-1] + ("A" if tok[-1] != "A" else "B"), "901-0001-A")
        ok("the token serves its own revision and no other, and a wrong token serves nothing",
           rc == 0 and o.strip().endswith("901-0001-A_kid-doc.pdf") and rc2 == 1 and rc3 == 1)
        mine = json.loads(run("library", "--viewer", wid)[1])
        own = json.loads(run("library", "--viewer", "owner")[1])
        with open(os.path.join(ROOT, "ws", wid, "register.json")) as fh:
            vtext = fh.read()
        ok("the owner is sent the token; the member and the member's view never are",
           own["documents"][1]["revisions"][0].get("token") == tok and tok not in json.dumps(mine) and tok not in vtext)
        run("public", "901-0001-A", "off")
        rc, o = run("token", tok, "901-0001-A")
        rc2, tok2 = run("public", "901-0001-A", "on")
        rc3, o3 = run("token", tok, "901-0001-A")
        ok("private deletes the token for good: the old one never serves again, and public again is a new one",
           rc == 1 and rc2 == 0 and tok2.strip() != tok and rc3 == 1 and run("token", tok2.strip(), "901-0001-A")[0] == 0)
        # DOCS_PUBLIC_HOOK: where the link is served hears on and off; off that can't reach it changes nothing
        hook, hlog = os.path.join(t, "hook.py"), os.path.join(t, "hook.log")
        with open(hook, "w") as fh:
            fh.write("import os, sys\nopen(sys.argv[1], 'a').write(' '.join(sys.argv[2:]) + '\\n')\n"
                     "if os.path.exists(sys.argv[1] + '.fail'): sys.exit('site unreachable')\n"
                     "print('https://lib.example/p/' + sys.argv[3])\n")
        os.environ["DOCS_PUBLIC_HOOK"] = f"{sys.executable} {hook} {hlog}"
        tok2 = tok2.strip()
        rc, o = run("public", "901-0001-A", "on")
        ok("with a hook, on hands it the token and prints the address it answers under the token",
           rc == 0 and o.splitlines() == [tok2, f"https://lib.example/p/{tok2}"]
           and open(hlog).read().splitlines() == [f"on {tok2} 901-0001-A"])
        open(hlog + ".fail", "w").close()
        rc, o = run("public", "901-0001-A", "off")
        ok("off whose hook fails refuses and keeps the token, so the link is never half revoked",
           rc == 2 and "still public" in o and run("token", tok2, "901-0001-A")[0] == 0)
        rc, o = run("public", "901-0001-A", "on")
        ok("on whose hook fails prints the token, exits 1 and keeps it for a retry",
           rc == 1 and o.splitlines()[0] == tok2 and "again retries" in o and run("token", tok2, "901-0001-A")[0] == 0)
        os.remove(hlog + ".fail")
        rc, o = run("public", "901-0001-A", "off")
        ok("off whose hook answers tells it the token first, then deletes it",
           rc == 0 and open(hlog).read().splitlines()[-1] == f"off {tok2} 901-0001-A"
           and run("token", tok2, "901-0001-A")[0] == 1)
        calls = len(open(hlog).read().splitlines())
        run("public", "901-0001-A", "off")
        ok("off on a revision with no token calls no hook", len(open(hlog).read().splitlines()) == calls)
        os.environ.pop("DOCS_PUBLIC_HOOK")
        # revisions: a register of its own
        ROOT = os.path.join(t, "r2")
        v1 = mkpdf(src, "v1", "Gamma first version")
        v2 = mkpdf(src, "v2", "Gamma second version")
        tex = os.path.join(src, "gamma.tex")
        run("file", v1, "--project", "Box", "--kind", "work", "--title", "Gamma", "--source", tex)
        rc, o = run("file", v1, "--project", "Box", "--title", "Gamma", "--source", tex)
        d = load()["documents"]["001-0001"]
        ok("the same content again files nothing and names the current revision",
           rc == 0 and "unchanged" in o and "001-0001-A" in o and len(d["revisions"]) == 1)
        rc, o = run("file", v2, "--project", "Box", "--title", "Gamma renamed", "--source", tex)
        d = load()["documents"]["001-0001"]
        ok("changed content from the same source is the next letter of the same number",
           rc == 0 and "001-0001-B" in o and [r["rev"] for r in d["revisions"]] == ["A", "B"] and len(load()["documents"]) == 1)
        ok("revision A's file is kept and not rewritten", os.path.isfile(os.path.join(ROOT, d["revisions"][0]["file"]))
           and "Gamma first" in pdftext(os.path.join(ROOT, d["revisions"][0]["file"])))
        rc, o = run("file", v1, "--project", "Box", "--title", "Gamma renamed")
        ok("the same title with no source is the same document too (C, not a new number)",
           "001-0001-C" in o and len(load()["documents"]) == 1)
        # --source on an unchanged rebuild: a session attaches a .tex it found after the PDF was filed
        ROOT = os.path.join(t, "r2d")
        alone2 = os.path.join(t, "alone2")
        os.makedirs(alone2)
        shutil.copy(mkpdf(src, "z1", "Zeta first version"), os.path.join(alone2, "z1.pdf"))
        z1 = os.path.join(alone2, "z1.pdf")
        run("file", z1, "--project", "Box", "--kind", "work", "--title", "Zeta")
        d = load()["documents"]["001-0001"]
        ok("filed with nothing findable keeps no source and packs nothing",
           d.get("source") is None and "sources" not in d["revisions"][0])
        found = os.path.join(alone2, "found.tex")
        with open(found, "w") as f:
            f.write("\\documentclass{article}\\begin{document}Zeta\\end{document}\n")
        rc, o = run("file", z1, "--project", "Box", "--title", "Zeta", "--source", found)
        d = load()["documents"]["001-0001"]
        ok("--source on an unchanged rebuild records the found source and packs it, filing no new revision",
